{"id": "37", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) (Passage 2).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper (Passage 1 and 2).\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet lined with butter-flavored cooking spray (Passage 1).\n4. Add onion, green pepper, and tomato slices to the baking sheet (Passage 1).\n5. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (Passage 1 and 2).\n6. To add cheesy flavor, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for an additional 3 minutes (Passage 3).\n\nNote that Passage 3 does not provide any specific instructions for cooking the pollock, but rather suggests adding cheese to the existing dish.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the type of pollock and its characteristics.\n- Determine the preferred cooking method for pollock, such as frying, baking, or grilling.\n- Gather necessary ingredients and cooking tools, such as olive oil, salt, pepper, and a frying pan or grill.\n- Prepare the pollock by cleaning and trimming any excess fat or skin, if desired.\n- Season the pollock with salt and pepper.\n- Heat the cooking oil in the frying pan or preheat the grill.\n- Place the pollock in the hot oil or on the grill.\n- Cook the pollock for the recommended time, which may vary depending on\nthe size and thickness of the fish.\n- Flip the pollock over halfway through cooking to ensure even browning.\n- Remove the pollock from the heat or grill when it is cooked to your desired level of doneness, typically when the flesh is opaque and flakes easily with a f