{"id": "47", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "gt": "To fold a quilt, follow these steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface such as a bed or table.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, ensuring the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, again on the bias.\n5. Finally, fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is also on the bias.", "pred": "To fold a quilt, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To fold a quilt, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of quilt and its size.\n2. Lay the quilt flat on a large, flat surface.\n3. Align the edges of the quilt to ensure it is even.\n4. Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, bringing the top and bottom edges together.\n5. Smooth out any wrinkles or creases as you fold.\n6. Fold the quilt in half again, this time widthwise, bringing the left and right sides together.\n7. Tuck the ends of the quilt into the folds to secure them.\n8. Align the corners of the quilt to ensure they are even.\n9. Press the quilt with a pressing tool or iron to ensure all folds are sharp and crisp.\n10. Fold the quilt in half diagonally, bringing the opposite corners together to create a triangular shape.\n11. Press the quilt along the fold to ensure it is smooth and tight.\n12. Tuck the ends of the quilt into the folds to secure them.\n13. Align the corners of the quilt to ensure they are even.\n14. Press the quilt again to ensure all folds are sharp and crisp.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of quilt and its size.\n2. Lay the quilt flat on a large, flat surface.\n3. Align the edges of the quilt to ensure it is even.\n4. Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, bringing the top and bottom edges together.\n5. Smooth out any wrinkles or creases as you fold.\n6. Fold the quilt in half again, this time widthwise, bringing the left and right sides together.\n7. Tuck the ends of the quilt into the folds to secure them.\n8. Align the corners of the quilt to ensure they are even.\n9. Press the quilt with\nThe next logical reasoning step is:\n10. Fold the quilt in half diagonally, bringing the opposite corners together to create a triangular shape.\n11. Press the quilt along the fold to ensure it is smooth and tight.\n12. Tuck the ends of the quilt into the folds to secure them.\n13. Align the corners of the quilt to ensure they are even.\n14. Press the quilt again to ensure all folds are sharp and crisp.\n\nAnswer: To fold a quilt, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of quilt and its size.\n2. Lay the quilt flat on a large, flat surface.\n3. Align the edges of the quilt to ensure it is even.\n4. Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, bringing the top and bottom edges together.\n5. Smooth out any wrinkles or creases as you fold.\n6. Fold the quilt in half again, this time widthwise, bringing the left and right sides together.\n7. Tuck the ends of the quilt into the folds to secure them.\n8. Align the corners of the quilt to ensure they are even.\n9. Press the quilt with a pressing tool or iron to ensure all folds are sharp and crisp.\n10. Fold the quilt in half diagonally, bringing the opposite corners together to create a triangular shape.\n11. Press the quilt along the fold to ensure it is smooth and tight.\n12. Tuck the ends of the quilt into the folds to secure them.\n13. Align the corners of the quilt to ensure they are even.\n14. Press the quilt again to ensure all folds are sharp and crisp.", "time_sec": 26.886, "generation_time_seconds": 26.8245, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0522, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 