{"id": "55", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "You can prevent birds from building nests on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch and the top of the porch if it has open rafters. This will block the birds from reaching spaces they often choose to build their nests. If you have a light fixture, you can also install bird netting over it, but make sure the netting is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs and doesn't entangle birds. Another method is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch, as this can scare birds away. Remember to move the plastic hawk periodically to prevent the birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the birds that are building nests on the porch.\n2. Determine the materials they are using to build their nests.\n3. Consider the behavior of these birds and their nesting habits.\n4. Research methods or deterrents that are effective in preventing birds from building nests in specific locations.\n5. Evaluate the feasibility of implementing the deterrents on the porch.\n6. Test the deterrents and monitor the results over a period of time. Answer:[Unable to answer based on given passages]\nThe reasoning steps are:\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 33.603, "generation_time_seconds": 33.5529, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0365, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 19654, 429, 525, 4752, 95121, 389, 279, 44647, 624, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 7236, 807, 525, 1667, 311, 1936, 862, 95121, 624, 18, 13, 21144, 279, 7709, 315, 1493, 19654, 323, 862, 66710, 25785,