{"id": "101", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Turn on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes.\n2. Download the audiobook you want from iTunes.\n3. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n4. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the left task pane of the iTunes window.\n5. Select the audiobook you want to sync by clicking on its title.\n6. Click \"Sync Audiobooks\" and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer.\n7. Click \"Apply\" to start the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your iPhone to iTunes. The software allows two-way transfer of files, so you can not only backup files to your PC but also transfer audiobooks from your PC to your iPhone. Here are the steps to use Syncios Audiobook Transfer:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n3. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer and click \"Export\" to save them to your computer.\n5. Alternatively, you can also click \"Import\" to add new audiobooks from your computer to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" to start the transfer process.\n\nNote that the above steps are based on the assumption that you have already turned on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes. If you have not done so, you will need to do so before attempting to sync your audiobooks.", "pred": "To sync an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To sync an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the source of the audiobook: Determine if the audiobook is stored on the iPhone or obtained from iTunes.\n2. Check if the audiobook is already in iTunes: Verify if the audiobook is already synchronized with iTunes on the computer.\n3. Connect the iPhone to the computer: Ensure that the iPhone is properly connected to the computer via USB.\n4. Open iTunes on the computer: Launch the iTunes application on the computer.\n5. Select the iPhone in iTunes: In iTunes, select the iPhone from the list of devices.\n6. Check the \"Books\" tab: Navigate to the \"Books\" tab in iTunes.\n7. Check the audiobook's availability in the \"Books\" tab: Look for the audiobook in the \"Books\" section under the iPhone device in iTunes. If it is not present, proceed to add it.\n8. Add the audiobook to iTunes if it is not already present: Click the \"+\" button in the \"Books\" tab to add the audiobook to your iTunes library.\n9. Transfer the audiobook to the iPhone: In the \"Books\" tab, select the audiobook and click the \"Sync\" button to transfer it to the iPhone.\n10. Verify the audiobook on the iPhone: Disconnect the iPhone from the computer and check if the audiobook is available on the iPhone. If it is not present, repeat steps 7-9. If it is present, the audiobook has been successfully synced from the iPhone to iTunes. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the source of the audiobook: Determine if the audiobook is stored on the iPhone or obtained from iTunes.\n2. Check if the audiobook is already in iTunes: Verify if the audiobook is already synchronized with iTunes on the computer.\n3. Connect the iPhone to the computer: Ensure that the iPhone is properly connected to the computer via USB.\n4. Open iTunes on the computer: Launch the iTunes application on the computer.\n5. Select the iPhone in iTunes: In iTunes, select the iPhone from the list of devices.\n6. Check the \"Books\" tab: Navigate to the \"Books\" tab in iTunes\nThe next logical reasoning step is:\n7. Check the audiobook's availability in the \"Books\" tab: Look for the audiobook in the \"Books\" section under the iPhone device in iTunes. If it is not present, proceed to add it.\n8. Add the audiobook to iTunes if it is not already present: Click the \"+\" button in the \"Books\" tab to add the audiobook to your iTunes library.\n9. Transfer the audiobook to the iPhone: In the \"Books\" tab, select the audiobook and click the \"Sync\" button to transfer it to the iPhone.\n10. Verify the audiobook on the iPhone: Disconnect the\n\nAnswer: To sync an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the source of the audiobook: Determine if the audiobook is stored on the iPhone or obtained from iTunes.\n2. Check if the audiobook is already in iTunes: Verify if the audiobook is already synchronized with iTunes on the computer.\n3. Connect the iPhone to the computer: Ensure that the iPhone is properly connected to the computer via USB.\n4. Open iTunes on the computer: Launch the iTunes application on the computer.\n5. Select the iPhone in iTunes: In iTunes, select the iPhone from the list of devices.\n6. Check the \"Books\" tab: Navigate to the \"Books\" tab in iTunes.\n7. Check the audiobook's availability in the \"Books\" tab: Look for the audiobook in the \"Books\" section under the iPhone device in iTunes. If it is not present, proceed to add it.\n8. Add the audiobook to iTunes if it is not already present: Click the \"+\" button in the \"Books\" tab to add the audiobook to your iTunes library.\n9. Transfer the audiobook to the iPhone: In the \"Books\" tab, select the audiobook and click the \"Sync\" button to transfer it to the iPhone.\n10. Verify the audiobook on the iPhone: Disconnect the iPhone from the computer and check if the audiobook is available on the iPhone. If it is not present, repeat steps 7-9. If it is present, the audiobook has been successfully synced from the iPhone to iTunes. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 34.426, "generation_time_seconds": 34.3811, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0349, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollo