{"id": "191", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "To attach multiple picture frames together, you can use small hinges to connect the frames. Lay the frames beside each other to determine the desired arrangement. For two frames, use identical ones, and for three frames, either choose three identical frames or use a larger one as the middle frame. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges. Attach the hinges to securely join the frames.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the types of picture frames being used - determine if they are all of the same type or if there are different styles or sizes of frames. This will affect the method of attachment.\n2. Assess the materials and construction of the frames - consider whether the frames are made of wood, metal, or plastic, as this can influence the choice of attachment method and the strength of the bond. Check if the frames have pre-drilled holes or require additional hardware such as screws, brackets, or adhesive.\n3. Determine the desired aesthetic and practical considerations - consider how the frames should look together, whether they should be aligned perfectly or with a slight gap, and whether the attachment should be visible or hidden. This will help in choosing the most appropriate attachment method.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 37.65, "generation_time_seconds": 37.5999, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0384, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645