{"id": "255", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 10.851, "generation_time_seconds": 10.8195, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0271, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645