{"id": "310", "question": "avg cost to install a second floor in a house", "gt": "Hiring a remodeling contractor to build a second floor addition can cost between $100-$300 a square foot for a typical addition, but the cost can go as high as $400-$500 per square foot depending on the complexity, quality of materials and local labor rates. Building a second floor can cost at least 20 percent more than building the same square footage at ground level.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Determine the size of the new floor to be installed.\n2. Consider the materials needed for the flooring, such as wood, concrete, or composite materials.\n3. Factor in the costs of labor for construction, including the time and expertise required to install the new floor.\n4. Account for any additional structural or plumbing work that may be necessary, such as reinforcing the existing floor joists or modifying the plumbing lines.\n5. Include any permit fees or inspections that may be required by local building codes.\n6. Add any costs for tools, equipment, and materials that are not already included in the above steps.\n7. Calculate\n8. Calculate the total cost by adding up all the costs determined in the previous steps.\nThe next logical reasoning step would be to gather specific information about the size of the new floor, the materials to be used, labor costs, and any additional work required. This information would be necessary to perform the calculations and provide an accurate estimate for the cost of installing a second floor in a house.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 13.012, "generation_time_seconds": 12.969, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0313, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout