{"id": "341", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ribs:\n\nStep 1: Prepare the ribs\n\n* Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs (passage 3)\n* Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard mixture (passage 2)\n\nStep 2: Grill the ribs\n\n* Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (passage 1)\n* Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush with some of the sauce (passage 1)\n* Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs with more sauce (passage 1)\n* Continue to cook and flip every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through (passage 1)\n\nTotal grilling time: 20 minutes\n\nNote: The passages do not mention the temperature at which to cook the ribs, but a medium heat of 350°F to 450°F is suggested.", "pred": "To make ribs, start by cutting the ribs into individual pieces. Season the ribs with a mixture of salt, pepper, and other desired spices. Marinate the ribs in the seasoning mixture for at least an hour, or overnight for better flavor. This initial preparation sets the foundation for achieving the best texture and flavor in the final dish.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ribs, start by cutting the ribs into individual pieces. Season the ribs with a mixture of salt, pepper, and other desired spices. Marinate the ribs in the seasoning mixture for at least an hour, or overnight for better flavor. This initial preparation sets the foundation for achieving the best texture and flavor in the final dish.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the main ingredients and tools needed for making ribs.\n2. Describe the initial preparation of the ribs, including cutting, seasoning, and marinating.\n3. Explain the cooking process, detailing the method (grilling, baking, or boiling) and the duration.\n4. Provide tips on achieving the best texture and flavor, such as the use of a smoker or basting.\n5. Summarize the final steps for serving and presentation.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n2. Describe the initial preparation of the ribs, including cutting, seasoning, and marinating.\n\nAnswer: To make ribs, start by cutting the ribs into individual pieces. Season the ribs with a mixture of salt, pepper, and other desired spices. Marinate the ribs in the seasoning mixture for at least an hour, or overnight for better flavor. This initial preparation sets the foundation for achieving the best texture and flavor in the final dish.", "time_sec": 19.908, "generation_time_seconds": 19.8654, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0349, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 1887, 13966, 25, 576, 1156, 3019, 304, 3259, 55149, 374, 311, 10542, 279, 1887, 13966, 2567, 369, 279, 11116, 13, 45302, 11, 279, 1887, 13966, 369, 3259, 55149, 525, 35067, 55149, 11, 12021, 11, 24353, 11, 323, 1008, 3200, 819, 1741, 438, 25298, 40454, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 476, 37327, 16723, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.9233, -0.0002, -0.0935, -0.0014, -0.8722, -0.1674, -1.6202, -0.8211, -1.7595, -0.0032, -0.3325, -0.0396, -0.0, -0.905, -0.0079, -0.2845, -0.0004, -0.0168, -0.0, -1.747, -1.3573, -0.0031, -0.5958, -0.0041, -0.5656, -0.0, -0.7498, -0.3371, -0.0038, -0.3213, -1.1972, -0.0, -2.3885, -0.888, -0.0476, -0.0102, -0.1732, -0.0001, -0.0438, -0.0, -0.0216, -1.2159, -0.0297, 0.0, -0.2362, 0.0, -0.8776, 0.0, -0.0169, -0.0254, -0.0645, -0.0, -2.6523, -0.0655, -0.0, -0.7453, -Infinity, -Infinity, -13.334, -5.8595, -7.5007, -23.9583, -4.5084, -6.3449, -6.5797, -0.3692, -10.3023, -6.4