{"id": "480", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 3: Explain the process of changing address with the U.S. Postal Service, including the necessary forms and fees.\nStep 4: Provide specific examples of the forms and fees required for changing an address with the U.S. Postal Service.\nStep 5: Describe the timeline for processing a change of address with the U.S. Postal Service, including how long it typically takes for mail to be redirected.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 14.289, "generation_time_seconds": 14.253, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0295, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.597, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0057, -0.0005, -24.2708, -17.5504, -3.1553, -6.0603, -7.8136, -8.5623, -10.0195, -8.3443, -7.1001, -6.305, -6.8106, -6.9196, -4.3228, -2.2323, -2.795, -4.205, -4.8283], "cumulative_logprob": -131.8995, "norm_logp": -4.8852, "input_len": 144, "output_tok