{"id": "519", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how raffles work:\n\n1. Reverse Raffle: In this type of raffle, the numbers on the entry tickets are drawn in reverse order, starting with the last number and ending with the first number. For example, if there are 55 entries, the last number drawn wins the grand prize, followed by the next-to-last number, and so on until the first number. Each entry ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket worth $1,000 and two $500 prizes (for the early bird drawing and the first ticket pulled).\n2. 50-50 Draw: This is a raffle held during a single day at a specific event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roving staff with handheld electronic devices. The gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool, and 50% of the prize pool is awarded to the winner of a random draw that takes place at the end of the event. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n3. Additional Raffles: In addition to the main raffle, there may be additional raffles for drinks and dinner. These raffles are not included in the original ticket price and require separate entry fees. One of these raffles offers the chance to win $10,000!\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of raffle: Determine whether the raffle is a traditional raffle, a prize draw, or any other type of raffle.\n2. Understand the entry process: Explain how participants enter the raffle, such as purchasing tickets or registering online.\n3. Explain the drawing process: Describe how the winning numbers or tickets are selected, including any rules or procedures.\n4. Discuss prize distribution: Outline how the prizes are awarded to the winners, including any rules or restrictions.\n5. Mention any additional rules: Highlight any specific rules or regulations for the raffle, such as age restrictions or eligibility criteria.\n6\n6. Discuss the role of the raffle organizer: Explain the responsibilities of the person or entity organizing the raffle, including managing entries, conducting the draw, and distributing prizes.\n7. Mention any legal considerations: Highlight any legal requirements or guidelines that the raffle organizer must follow, such as state or local laws regarding gambling or fundraising.\n8. Describe the outcome and impact: Explain the potential outcomes of participating in the raffle and how the experience may impact the participants, such as the possibility of winning a prize or the excitement of the draw.\n9. Discuss any potential risks or downsides: Highlight any potential risks or downsides\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 24.172, "generation_time_seconds": 24.128, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0354, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17, 13, 64547, 279, 1376, 6813, 315, 264, 14260, 435, 44090, 25, 14403, 11, 37408, 11, 323, 264, 13330, 1882, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 15