ens": 122}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "657", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly.\n3. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\n4. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n5. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n6. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n7. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles.\n8. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\n\nTherefore, the steps to properly clean your hair are:\n\n1. Choose the right products.\n2. Wet your hair.\n3. Shampoo your hair.\n4. Rinse and detangle.\n5. Condition your hair.\n6. Rinse and comb.\n7. Dry your hair with a towel.\n8. Use a hair dryer.", "pred": "After rinsing the conditioner out of your hair, gently towel-dry your hair to remove excess water. Avoid rubbing your hair too hard, as this can cause breakage. Instead, use a wide-tooth comb to detangle your hair while it's still damp. Once your hair is mostly dry, you can use a hair dryer on a low heat setting, but be careful not to overheat your hair. Finally, style your hair as desired, using a heat protectant spray if you plan to use heat styling tools. Regularly trimming your hair can also help maintain its health and appearance.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: After rinsing the conditioner out of your hair, gently towel-dry your hair to remove excess water. Avoid rubbing your hair too hard, as this can cause breakage. Instead, use a wide-tooth comb to detangle your hair while it's still damp. Once your hair is mostly dry, you can use a hair dryer on a low heat setting, but be careful not to overheat your hair. Finally, style your hair as desired, using a heat protectant spray if you plan to use heat styling tools. Regularly trimming your hair can also help maintain its health and appearance.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Begin by gathering all necessary supplies for hair cleaning, such as shampoo, conditioner, a wide-tooth comb, and a clean towel.\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly with warm water, ensuring that all sections are saturated.\n3. Apply a generous amount of shampoo to your scalp, working it into a lather. Focus on massaging the scalp gently to help loosen dirt, oil, and product buildup.\n4. Rinse the shampoo out of your hair, making sure to remove all suds and residue.\n5. Apply conditioner to the mid-lengths and ends of your hair, avoiding the roots. This helps to det\nThe reasoning steps are:\nPlease generate the NEXT logical reasoning step. Do NOT provide the final answer yet. Focus strictly on analyzing the physical details step by step.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: After rinsing the conditioner out of your hair, gently towel-dry your hair to remove excess water. Avoid rubbing your hair too hard, as this can cause breakage. Instead, use a wide-tooth comb to detangle your hair while it's still damp. Once your hair is mostly dry, you can use a hair dryer on a low heat setting, but be careful not to overheat your hair. Finally, style your hair as desired, using a heat protectant spray if you plan to use heat styling tools. Regularly trimming your hair can also help maintain its health and appearance.", "time_sec": 46.829, "generation_time_seconds": 46.7796, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0377, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645,