{"id": "709", "question": "what do the colors of the tennessee flag mean", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe colors of the Tennessee flag have the following meanings:\n\n* White represents purity\n* Blue represents patriotism\n* Red represents the willingness to shed blood during warfare\n\nThe three white stars on the flag represent the three grand divisions of Tennessee: East, Middle, and West. The blue field with the white stars is meant to symbolize the three divisions bound together as one.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the colors present on the Tennessee flag.\n- Research the historical and symbolic meanings of these colors in the context of the flag's design and the state's history.\n- Provide a detailed explanation of each color's significance, supported by relevant historical facts or symbols associated with the Tennessee flag.\nThe colors present on the Tennessee flag are red, white, and blue. These colors are also present in the American flag.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 21.022, "generation_time_seconds": 20.9835, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0314, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 576, 21085, 3897, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 1995, 911, 279, 23219, 5181, 476, 1181, 7987, 624, 17, 13, 576, 3405, 17064, 369, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 7987, 389, 279, 23219, 5181, 624, 18, 13, 17147, 279, 9760, 1995, 504, 279, 21085, 11, 279, 3383, 374, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 4586, 6540, 911, 5181, 7987, 323, 862, 49700, 624, 19, 13, 576, 23219, 1584, 5181, 17167, 315, 264, 2070, 315, 6303, 448, 279, 1584, 22875, 315, 11715, 304, 279, 4126, 6