{"id": "57", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "pred": "To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting or bird spikes. These can be installed around the porch to prevent birds from landing and nesting. Additionally, you can use deterrents like ultrasonic devices or visual deterrents like reflective tape or plastic bottles. Regularly cleaning up any food or debris that might attract birds can also help prevent nesting. If these methods are not effective, you may need to consider professional pest control services. Remember to always ensure that any method you use is humane and does not harm the birds. Answer:[your answer here]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting or bird spikes. These can be installed around the porch to prevent birds from landing and nesting. Additionally, you can use deterrents like ultrasonic devices or visual deterrents like reflective tape or plastic bottles. Regularly cleaning up any food or debris that might attract birds can also help prevent nesting. If these methods are not effective, you may need to consider professional pest control services. Remember to always ensure that any method you use is humane and does not harm the birds. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the problem: Birds are building nests on the porch.\n2. Consider the environment: The porch is likely an outdoor, elevated area accessible to birds.\n3. Research methods to prevent nesting: Look for solutions that can be applied to the porch to deter birds from nesting.\n4. Evaluate potential solutions: Consider physical barriers, deterrents, and other methods.\n5. Select an appropriate solution: Choose a method that is effective, easy to implement, and safe for the birds and the house.\n6. Implement the solution: Apply the chosen method to prevent birds from nesting on the porch.\n7. Monitor the results: Check\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting or bird spikes. These can be installed around the porch to prevent birds from landing and nesting. Additionally, you can use deterrents like ultrasonic devices or visual deterrents like reflective tape or plastic bottles. Regularly cleaning up any food or debris that might attract birds can also help prevent nesting. If these methods are not effective, you may need to consider professional pest control services. Remember to always ensure that any method you use is humane and does not harm the birds. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 47.418, "generation_time_seconds": 47.3691, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0386, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 3838, 525, 1045, 4185, 5413, 1251, 990, 311, 5358, 19654, 504, 66710, 389, 862, 4154, 8528, 30, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1