{"id": "80", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is unknown. However, it is believed to be a result of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in communication between the brain and the GI tract, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors may include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (either too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps that worsen after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, as well as a lot of gas or bloating.", "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of IBS include stress, certain foods, and hormonal changes. Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of IBS include stress, certain foods, and hormonal changes. Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of IBS include stress, certain foods, and hormonal changes. Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of IBS include stress, certain foods, and hormonal changes. Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of IBS include stress, certain foods, and hormonal changes. Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of IBS include stress, certain foods, and hormonal changes. Answer: Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, gas, diarrhea, and constipation. Causes or triggers of 