{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the relevant information from the given passage about the treatment of an asset when it is discarded under the Income Tax Act.\n2. Analyze the specific details provided in the passage regarding the tax implications and any relevant sections of the Income Tax Act.\n3. Provide a clear and concise answer based on the information given, ensuring that it is supported by the details provided in the passage.\nTo answer the question about the treatment of an asset discarded under the Income Tax Act, we need to identify the relevant sections of the Act and any specific instructions or guidelines provided in the given passages. Let's break down the information step by step:\nTo continue with the logical reasoning steps:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 17.714, "generation_time_seconds": 17.6816, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0263, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516