{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "The final step in washing wine glasses properly is to dry the glass with a lint-free cloth or air dry it to prevent water spots.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The final step in washing wine glasses properly is to dry the glass with a lint-free cloth or air dry it to prevent water spots.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the specific type of wine glass being washed.\n2. Determine the level of dirtiness and any specific stains or residues present on the glass.\n3. Assess the available cleaning tools and cleaning solutions.\n4. Prepare the cleaning solution according to the instructions on the product label or based on personal preference.\n5. Rinse the glass thoroughly under cold water to remove loose particles and debris.\n6. Dip the glass into the cleaning solution, ensuring that the solution covers the entire surface of the glass.\n7. Swirl the glass gently in the solution to loosen and dissolve any remaining dirt or residue.\n8. Use a clean,\nscrub brush or soft cloth to gently scrub the glass, focusing on any stubborn stains or residues.\n9. Rinse the glass again under cold water to remove any remaining cleaning solution.\n10. Dry the glass with a lint-free cloth or air dry it to prevent water spots.\nAnswer: The final step in washing wine glasses properly is to dry the glass with a lint-free cloth or air dry it to prevent water spots.\n\nAnswer: The final step in washing wine glasses properly is to dry the glass with a lint-free cloth or air dry it to prevent water spots.", "time_sec": 16.78, "generation_time_seconds": 16.7433, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0299, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 3151, 943, 315, 13078, 8991, 1660, 37493, 624, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 2188, 315, 25284, 1880, 323, 894, 3151, 62463, 476, 70683, 3042, 389, 279, 8991, 624, 18, 13, 81835, 279, 2500, 15826, 7375, 323, 15826, 9904, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 279, 15826, 6291, 4092, 311, 279, 11221, 389, 279, 1985, 2383, 476, 3118, 389, 4345, 21933, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 8991, 26364, 1212, 9255, 3015, 311, 4057, 20174, 18730, 323, 33998, 624, 21, 13, 55047, 279, 8991, 1119, 279, 15826, 6291, 11, 22573, 429, 279, 6291, 14521, 279, 4453, 7329, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 22, 13, 4492, 2811, 279, 8991, 29273, 304, 279, 6291, 311, 82742, 323, 72639, 894, 9664, 25284, 476, 48132, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 264, 4240, 11], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.1587, -0.0002, -0.1707, -0.0027, -2.0422, -1.5542, -0.0122, -0.0059, -0.3027, -1.9525, -1.1781, -0.7526, -0.0243, 0.0, -0.5357, -0.1433, -0.4757, -0.0, -0.4347, -0.0262, -2.2789, -0.8356, -0.2626, -0.0306, -2.2706, -0.227, -0.7581, -0.4303, -0.0, -0.0379, -0.0092, -0.0001, 0.0, -3.154, -0.1195, -0.6216, -0.3215, -0.0511, -0.0137, -3.0255, -1.9007, -0.6381, -0.0002, 0.0, -2.0176, -0.0546, -0.0126, -0.098, -1.4169, 0.0, -0.0128, -1.0527, -1.8534, -0.0103, -0.1541, -0.9246, -0.2625, -0.3673, 0.0, -0.6563, -0.1799, -0.2028, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.4267, 0.0, -0.0, -0.5083, -1.6372, -0.925, -2.5494, -0.1198, -0.0105, -0.0069, -1.2095, -1.452, -0.5125, -1.014, -0.0019, -0.0001, 0.0, -3.4001, -0.0527, -0.0887, -0.0537, -0.0036, -0.2558