{"id": "287", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325 degrees F. Place the frozen roast in a roasting pan and rub the surface with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and desired seasonings. Place the roast, uncovered, in the preheated oven. Cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound or until the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees F. Once cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, first preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Place the frozen pork loin roast in the oven and cook for approximately 20-25 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 145°F (63°C). For example, if the pork loin roast weighs 2 pounds, it should be cooked for about 40-50 minutes. After cooking, let the pork loin roast rest for 10-15 minutes before slicing and serving. Answer:[your answer here]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, first preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Place the frozen pork loin roast in the oven and cook for approximately 20-25 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 145°F (63°C). For example, if the pork loin roast weighs 2 pounds, it should be cooked for about 40-50 minutes. After cooking, let the pork loin roast rest for 10-15 minutes before slicing and serving. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the type of meat: frozen pork loin roast.\n2. Determine the cooking method: oven.\n3. Consider the initial state of the meat: frozen.\n4. Assess the need for preheating the oven.\n5. Decide on the appropriate cooking time and temperature.\n6. Identify any necessary preparation steps (e.g., thawing, seasoning).\n7. Consider any additional cooking techniques that may be required (e.g., basting, covering).\n8. Evaluate the final presentation or serving suggestions.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to consider the initial state of the meat and the necessity of preheating the oven before cooking the frozen pork loin roast.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, first preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Place the frozen pork loin roast in the oven and cook for approximately 20-25 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 145°F (63°C). For example, if the pork loin roast weighs 2 pounds, it should be cooked for about 40-50 minutes. After cooking, let the pork loin roast rest for 10-15 minutes before slicing and serving. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 42.714, "generation_time_seconds": 42.6447, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0537, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 510, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 13041, 25, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 624, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 17233, 1714, 25, 23387, 624, 18, 13, 21144, 279, 2856, 1584, 315, 279, 13041, 25, 19690, 624, 19, 13, 81835, 279, 1184, 369, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 98881, 389, 279, 8311, 17233, 882, 323, 9315, 624, 21, 13, 64547, 894, 5871, 17975, 7354, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 85378, 287, 11, 86219, 4292, 22, 13, 21144, 894, 5107, 17233, 12538, 429, 1231, 387, 2567, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 293, 14725, 11, 18202, 4292, 23, 13, 54115, 279, 1590, 15496, 476, 13480, 18225, 382], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.3243, -0.0198, -0.0002, -0.0, -3.3092, -0.0019, -0.0001, -0.2825, -0.001, -0.2158, -0.0067, -0.1035, -0.2927, -3.2212, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.4293, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0328, -0.0002, -0.011, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0093, -0.0491, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.4983, -0.037, -0.7232, -0.0418, -0.0155, -0.0, -0.0442, -0.0436, -0.0019, -0.0286, -0.0004, 0.0, -1.7161, -0.0825, -0.5149, -0.0036, -3.0522, -0.0476, -0.0, -