{"id": "428", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. They can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning they develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning they develop from two different eggs with each being fertilized by its own sperm cell. Monoamniotic twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization. Dizygotic twin pregnancies are more likely in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, aged between 30 and 40 years, of above average height and weight, and who have had several previous pregnancies.", "pred": "Twins can happen through different processes, including single-embryo and multiple-embryo fertilization. Single-embryo fertilization results in identical twins, where both embryos develop from a single fertilized egg. Multiple-embryo fertilization can lead to fraternal twins, where two separate eggs are fertilized by two sperm, resulting in two different genetic individuals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Twins can happen through different processes, including single-embryo and multiple-embryo fertilization. Single-embryo fertilization results in identical twins, where both embryos develop from a single fertilized egg. Multiple-embryo fertilization can lead to fraternal twins, where two separate eggs are fertilized by two sperm, resulting in two different genetic individuals.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n- Twins can happen through different processes, including single-embryo and multiple-embryo fertilization.\n- Single-embryo fertilization results in identical twins, where both embryos develop from a single fertilized egg.\n- Multiple-embryo fertilization can lead to fraternal twins, where two separate eggs are fertilized by two sperm, resulting in two different genetic individuals.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n- Twins can happen through different processes, including single-embryo and multiple-embryo fertilization.\n- Single-embryo fertilization results in identical twins, where both embryos develop from a single fertilized egg.\n- Multiple-embryo fertilization can lead to fraternal twins, where two separate eggs are fertilized by two sperm, resulting in two different genetic individuals.\n\nAnswer: Twins can happen through different processes, including single-embryo and multiple-embryo fertilization. Single-embryo fertilization results in identical twins, where both embryos develop from a single fertilized egg. Multiple-embryo fertilization can lead to fraternal twins, where two separate eggs are fertilized by two sperm, resulting in two different genetic individuals.", "time_sec": 25.743, "generation_time_seconds": 25.6989, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0384, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.4328, -0.0206, -0.0006, -0