{"id": "520", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA reverse raffle works by having participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, usually between 1 and 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table consists of 20 individuals who pool their money together to form a complete ticket worth $1000. There are also two $500 prizes, one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\n\nThe 50-50 draw is a raffle that takes place during a single event, where tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roaming staff. 50% of the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, and the winner of the random draw at the end of the event receives 50% of the prize pool. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n\nFinally, some events may include cash tip board raffles, where participants can pay to play and have the chance to win $10,000. These raffles are not included in the ticket price.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the key components or aspects of a raffle mentioned in the passage.\n- Explain how these components or aspects work together to facilitate a raffle.\n- Provide an example or scenario to illustrate the process.\n- Ensure all details from the passage are utilized to construct the answer.\n- Identify the key components or aspects of a raffle mentioned in the passage.\nExplain how these components or aspects work together to facilitate a raffle.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 9.072, "generation_time_seconds": 9.0343, "selection_time_seconds": 0.032, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 1249, 8253, 1246, 435, 80535, 975, 1