{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "SMS allows for the sending and receiving of text messages, while MMS allows for the sending and receiving of multimedia messages, such as images, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be much longer and can include a variety of multimedia content. SMS messages are typically sent using cellular networks, while MMS messages can be sent over cellular networks as well as other types of networks, such as Wi-Fi.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: SMS allows for the sending and receiving of text messages, while MMS allows for the sending and receiving of multimedia messages, such as images, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be much longer and can include a variety of multimedia content. SMS messages are typically sent using cellular networks, while MMS messages can be sent over cellular networks as well as other types of networks, such as Wi-Fi.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nFirst, identify the key differences between SMS and MMS. SMS stands for Short Message Service, while MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service. SMS allows for the sending and receiving of text messages, whereas MMS allows for the sending and receiving of multimedia messages, such as images, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be much longer and can include a variety of multimedia content. SMS messages are typically sent using cellular networks, while MMS messages can be sent over cellular networks as well as other types of networks, such as Wi-Fi.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: SMS allows for the sending and receiving of text messages, while MMS allows for the sending and receiving of multimedia messages, such as images, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be much longer and can include a variety of multimedia content. SMS messages are typically sent using cellular networks, while MMS messages can be sent over cellular networks as well as other types of networks, such as Wi-Fi.", "time_sec": 21.752, "generation_time_seconds": 21.7043, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0393, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -2.0294, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0041, -0.0004, -2