{"id": "20", "question": "how to grill a porterhouse", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain any information or instructions on how to grill a Porterhouse steak specifically. While they do provide general guidance on setting up a grill and preparing the grill grate, they do not offer any specific advice or steps for cooking a Porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot provide a response based on the given passages.", "pred": "To grill a porterhouse steak, preheat the grill to a high temperature of around 450-500°F (230-260°C). Season the steak with olive oil, salt, pepper, and herbs or spices. Grill the steak for approximately 2-3 minutes per side for medium-rare, using a meat thermometer to ensure the internal temperature reaches 135°F (57°C). Let the steak rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To grill a porterhouse steak, preheat the grill to a high temperature of around 450-500°F (230-260°C). Season the steak with olive oil, salt, pepper, and herbs or spices. Grill the steak for approximately 2-3 minutes per side for medium-rare, using a meat thermometer to ensure the internal temperature reaches 135°F (57°C). Let the steak rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the type of meat: A porterhouse steak is a cut of beef that consists of both the tenderloin and the strip loin.\n2. Determine the thickness of the steak: A typical porterhouse steak is about 2-3 inches thick.\n3. Preheat the grill: Heat your grill to a high temperature, around 450-500°F (230-260°C), to sear the meat quickly.\n4. Season the steak: Rub the porterhouse steak with olive oil and season it with salt, pepper, and your favorite herbs or spices.\n5. Grill\n6. Grill the steak: Place the seasoned porterhouse steak onto the preheated grill and cook for approximately 2-3 minutes per side for medium-rare. Use a meat thermometer to ensure the internal temperature reaches 135°F (57°C) for medium-rare.\n7. Rest the steak: Once cooked, remove the steak from the grill and let it rest for 5-10 minutes to allow the juices to redistribute throughout the meat.\n8. Slice and serve: Slice the steak against the grain and serve it with your preferred sides.\n\nAnswer: To grill a porterhouse steak, preheat the grill to a high temperature of around 450-500°F (230-260°C). Season the steak with olive oil, salt, pepper, and herbs or spices. Grill the steak for approximately 2-3 minutes per side for medium-rare, using a meat thermometer to ensure the internal temperature reaches 135°F (57°C). Let the steak rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "time_sec": 47.0, "generation_time_seconds": 46.5476, "selection_time_seconds": 0.404, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 29901, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 39058, 323, 279, 1372, 315, 4087, 9810, 498, 1366, 311, 4296, 624, 17, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 311, 264, 1550, 9315, 320, 19454, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 476, 220, 17, 18, 15, 30937, 4292, 18, 13, 14263, 279, 4087, 9810, 448, 12021, 11, 24353, 11, 323, 894, 1008, 12685, 3200, 819, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 4087, 9810, 525, 518, 3054, 9315, 1573, 1081, 9400, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 4087, 9810, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 9380, 1045, 3550, 1948, 1105, 311, 2138, 369, 1496, 17233, 624, 20, 13, 49848, 279, 4087, 9810, 369, 13187, 220, 18, 12, 19, 4420, 817, 3108, 369, 11051, 3795, 546, 1513, 23709, 11, 476, 7500, 279, 17233, 882, 4092, 311, 697, 14890, 2188], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.2481, -0.0002, -3.3685, -0.0076, -0.8295, -1.502, -0.0011, -2.4244, -0.707, -0.0202, -1.2478, -0.0001, -0.074, 0.0, -1.43, -0.5198, -0.0, -0.1181, -0.1804, -0.0086, 0.0, -0.0906, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0, -0.0007, -0.321, -0.033, -0.0789, -0.466, -0.0236, -0.0