{"id": "58", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "pred": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting, screens, or plastic sheeting. These barriers can effectively stop birds from accessing the porch and building nests. Additionally, removing any food sources or nesting materials near the porch can also discourage birds from nesting there.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting, screens, or plastic sheeting. These barriers can effectively stop birds from accessing the porch and building nests. Additionally, removing any food sources or nesting materials near the porch can also discourage birds from nesting there.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the problem: The problem is that birds are building nests on the porch, which is likely causing inconvenience or damage.\n2. Understand the context: The question is asking for a solution to prevent birds from building nests on the porch.\n3. Analyze the options: To provide a comprehensive answer, we need to consider different methods that can be used to prevent birds from nesting on the porch.\n4. Consider the effectiveness of each method: Evaluate the potential effectiveness of each method based on the information provided in the passages.\n5. Provide a clear and concise answer: Once the most effective methods have been identified, provide a clear\nAnswer: Prevent birds from building a nest on your porch by using physical barriers such as netting, screens, or plastic sheeting. These barriers can effectively stop birds from accessing the porch and building nests. Additionally, removing any food sources or nesting materials near the porch can also discourage birds from nesting there.\nAnswer: To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting, screens, or plastic sheeting. These barriers can effectively stop birds from accessing the porch and building nests. Additionally, removing any food sources or nesting materials near the porch can also discourage birds from nesting there.\n\nAnswer: To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can use physical barriers such as netting, screens, or plastic sheeting. These barriers can effectively stop birds from accessing the porch and building nests. Additionally, removing any food sources or nesting materials near the porch can also discourage birds from nesting there.", "time_sec": 31.937, "generation_time_seconds": 31.8828, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0421, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [