{"id": "120", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the context: The question asks about the meaning of the name \"Teresa.\"\n2. Analyze the provided information: The passage does not contain any details about the meaning of the name \"Teresa.\"\n3. Determine the next logical step: Since there is no information in the passage about the meaning of \"Teresa,\" the logical next step is to conclude that the answer cannot be derived from the given information.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 15.956, "generation_time_seconds": 15.9171, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0315, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 2266, 25, 576, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 330, 51, 37586, 10040, 17, 13, 37427, 2986, 279, 3897, 1995, 25, 576, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 3565, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 330, 51, 37586, 10040, 18, 13, 29901, 279, 1790, 19819, 3019, 25, 8704, 1052, 374, 902, 1995, 304, 279, 21085, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 330, 51, 37586, 1335, 279, 19819, 1790, 3019, 374, 311, 31094, 429, 279, 4226, 4157, 387, 14257, 504, 27