{"id": "141", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the given information, the passage mentions the treatment of an asset when it is discarded under the Income Tax Act. The passage does not provide specific details on the treatment, such as whether it involves deductions or other financial adjustments. Therefore, the appropriate next step is to look for additional information or context that could clarify the treatment of an asset discarded under the Income Tax Act. This could include searching for specific sections of the Income Tax Act, consulting tax regulations, or reviewing case law that addresses similar situations. Without this additional information, it is not possible to provide a comprehensive answer.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 17.951, "generation_time_seconds": 17.9021, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0394, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.6245, -0.0924, -0.0013, -0.0001, -1.5687, -Infinity, -14.1564, -11.6668, -6.6753, -12.429, -8.6258, -7.3572, -7.9522, -5.8906, -2.5528, -0.9347, -1.5574, -1.9228, -0.9535, -0.4395, -0.745, -1.0233, -1.0666, -2.2823, -1.5954, -2.6117, -2.4026, -1.3524, -0.5153, -1.3527, -3.1787, -6.254, -9.1684, -7.9183, -3.7777, -2.9841, -1.356, -4.3903, -6.4608, -5.424, -3.1761, -1.5179, -0.9363, -1.2046, -2.778, -6.0477, -4.1865, -2.9761, -3.576, -5.0123, -6.2544, -5.4266, -3.9873, -1.6808, -1.0673, -1.0634, -2.2044, -2.2045, -1.8438, -1.6726, -1.5069, -3.7766, -5.4249, -5.8418, -7.9187, -6.8799, -2.8008, -0.725, -0.1306, -0.1771, -1.8439, -2.7772, -2.2085, -2.395, -3.9799, -5.0092, -6.0457, -4.1835, -2.7761, -3.