{"id": "194", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding (Passage 1).\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect (Passage 1).\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, making sure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame (Passage 1).\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames (Passage 1).\n5. Test ideas by laying the group of multiple pictures out on the floor first (Passage 2).\n6. Screw the frame to the backer board, repeat with each frame, and attach a hanging wire to the back (Passage 3).\n\nIt's important to note that the passages do not provide specific information on how to attach multiple frames together other than the steps mentioned above. Therefore, if more detailed instructions are needed, it may be best to consult additional resources or seek advice from a professional framer.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of picture frames: Different types of picture frames may have different attachment methods. Some frames may be designed to be stacked vertically or horizontally, while others may require specific hardware or techniques to be joined together.\n\n2. Check the frame's construction: Examine the materials and construction of the frames. Some frames may be made of lightweight materials that require a different attachment method than heavier frames. Additionally, some frames may have pre-drilled holes or slots that can be used to secure them together.\n\n3. Determine the desired orientation: Decide whether you want to stack the frames vertically or horizontally. This will affect the attachment method.\n\n4. Choose the appropriate attachment method: Based on the type of frames and their construction, select the most suitable attachment method. For example, if you have frames with pre-drilled holes, you can use small picture frame screws or nails to join them together. If the frames have a lip or groove, you can use picture frame hangers or clips to attach them. For heavier frames, you may need to use picture frame clips or brackets to ensure stability.\n\n5. Assemble the frames: Carefully align the frames and insert the chosen attachment method to join them together. Make sure the frames are level and properly aligned before securing them.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of picture frames: Different types of picture frames may have different attachment methods. Some frames may be designed to be stacked vertically or horizontally, while others may require specific hardware or techniques to be joined together.\n2. Check the frame's construction: Examine the materials and construction of the frames. Some frames may be made of lightweight materials that require a different attachment method than heavier frames. Additionally, some frames may have pre-drilled holes or slots that can be used to secure them together.\n3. Determine the desired orientation: Decide whether you want to stack the frames vertically or horizontally. This will affect the attachment method\n3. Choose the appropriate attachment method: Based on the type of frames and their construction, select the most suitable attachment method. For example, if you have frames with pre-drilled holes, you can use small picture frame screws or nails to join them together. If the frames have a lip or groove, you can use picture frame hangers or clips to attach them. For heavier frames, you may need to use picture frame clips or brackets to ensure stability.\n4. Assemble the frames: Carefully align the frames and insert the chosen attachment method to join them together. Make sure the frames are level and properly aligned before securing them\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of picture frames: Different types of picture frames may have different attachment methods. Some frames may be designed to be stacked vertically or horizontally, while others may require specific hardware or techniques to be joined together.\n\n2. Check the frame's construction: Examine the materials and construction of the frames. Some frames may be made of lightweight materials that require a different attachment method than heavier frames. Additionally, some frames may have pre-drilled holes or slots that can be used to secure them together.\n\n3. Determine the desired orientation: Decide whether you want to stack the frames vertically or horizontally. This will affect the attachment method.\n\n4. Choose the appropriate attachment method: Based on the type of frames and their construction, select the most suitable attachment method. For example, if you have frames with pre-drilled holes, you can use small picture frame screws or nails to join them together. If the frames have a lip or groove, you can use picture frame hangers or clips to attach them. For heavier frames, you may need to use picture frame clips or brackets to ensure stability.\n\n5. Assemble the frames: Carefully align the frames and insert the chosen attachment method to join them together. Make sure the frames are level and properly aligned before securing them.", "time_sec": 24.45, "generation_time_seconds": 24.3726, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0649, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 4494, 315, 6802, 14087, 429, 1184, 311, 387, 12392, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 14087, 448, 20704, 11773, 11, 14087, 448, 264, 24668, 11, 14087, 448, 264, 4034, 1717, 288