{"id": "257", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the main components of the dryer vent that need cleaning.\n2. Determine the tools and materials required for cleaning the dryer vent.\n3. Describe the process of cleaning each component of the dryer vent.\n4. Provide specific instructions for removing and cleaning the lint filter.\n5. Explain how to clean the inside of the dryer vent duct.\n6. Mention any additional steps or safety precautions necessary for cleaning the dryer vent.\n7. Summarize the steps to ensure a complete and thorough cleaning of the dryer vent.\n4. Provide specific instructions for removing and cleaning the lint filter.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 28.022, "generation_time_seconds": 27.9508, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0647, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 1887, 6813, 315, 279, 46622, 10378, 429, 1184, 15826, 624, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 7375, 323, 7236, 2567, 369, 15826, 279, 46622, 10378, 624, 18, 13, 60785, 279, 1882, 315, 15826, 1817, 3692, 315, 279, 46622, 10378, 624, 19, 13, 39565, 3151, 11221, 369, 17592, 323, 15826, 279, 57920, 4051, 624, 20, 13, 81917, 1246, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 46622, 10378, 44239, 624, 21, 13, 85148, 894, 5107, 7354, 476, 7149, 59903, 5871, 369, 15826, 279, 46622, 10378, 624, 22, 13, 8116, 5612, 551, 279, 7354, 311, 5978, 264, 4583, 323, 17423, 15826, 315, 279, 46622, 10378, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.4644, -0.0001, -0.1795, -0.0012, -2.43, -0.4816, -0.0209, -1.3443, -0.0129, -0.0163, -1.8277, -0.017, -0.0356, -0.093, -0.0241, 0.0, -0.567, -0.0035, -0.4712, -0.3181, -0.0055, -0.1429, -0.0006, -0.0355, -0.8036, -0.003, -0.0, -0.004, -0.0002, 0.0, -1.0302, -0.0007, -0.1078, -0.0127, -0.415, -1.6688, -0.0548, -0.4138, 0.0, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0353, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.2672, -1.0804, -0.6235, -0.6315, -2.3081, -0.4528, -0.0414, -0.0499, -1.2025, -0.8733, -0.0473, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2643, -0.0795, -0.0, -0.2937, -0.0054, -2.0352, -0.0018, -0.0, -0.0164, -0.0128, -0.3233, -0.0776, -0.0001, 0.0, -2.731, -0.3244, -0.5821, -1.2789, -1.0209, -3.3302, -0.0199, -0.6667, -1.5071, -0.4241, -0.1183, -0.0046, -0.0, -0.1893, -0.0019, 0.0, -0.6375, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -2.8986, -2.1656, -0.0082, -0.4832, -2.6701, -0.1795, -0.4486, -0.0009, -0.0298, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1922, -0.0565], "cumulative_logprob": -46.7014, "norm_logp": -0.4406, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 106}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645,