{"id": "289", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\nPassage 1 states to defrost the roast first and then place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour. After taking it out, season the roast and turn the oven temperature to 350°F. Cook for 1.5 to 3 hours, depending on the size of the roast, making sure it's cooked all the way through.\n\nPassage 2 provides specific instructions for preparing the roast before cooking. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and any desired herbs. Place the roast in a preheated oven at 325°F and determine the cooking time based on the weight of the roast.\n\nPassage 3 suggests starting by preheating the oven to 350°F and then placing the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on a roasting rack. Cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, inserting a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature once cooked. Once the temperature reaches 150°F, remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.\n\nBased on these passages, the general steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are:\n\n1. Defrost the roast if not already thawed.\n2. Season the roast with salt, pepper, and herbs.\n3. Place the roast in a preheated oven at the appropriate temperature (250°F or 325°F) for the specified time.\n4. Check the internal temperature of the roast using a meat thermometer to ensure it reaches the desired doneness.\n5. Remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.", "pred": "9. When the internal temperature of the pork loin roast reaches the desired level (usually 145°F or 63°C for medium-rare), remove it from the oven and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: 9. When the internal temperature of the pork loin roast reaches the desired level (usually 145°F or 63°C for medium-rare), remove it from the oven and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Determine the weight and size of the frozen pork loin roast.\n2. Preheat the oven to a suitable temperature.\n3. Thaw the pork loin roast in the refrigerator or microwave.\n4. Season the pork loin roast with salt, pepper, and other desired spices.\n5. Place the seasoned pork loin roast on a baking sheet or roasting pan.\n6. Insert a meat thermometer into the thickest part of the roast to monitor the internal temperature.\n7. Cook the pork loin roast in the preheated oven at the determined temperature.\n8. Check the internal temperature of the pork loin roast regularly using the meat thermometer\nAnswer: 9. When the internal temperature of the pork loin roast reaches the desired level (usually 145°F or 63°C for medium-rare), remove it from the oven and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: 9. When the internal temperature of the pork loin roast reaches the desired level (usually 145°F or 63°C for medium-rare), remove it from the oven and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "time_sec": 27.236, "generation_time_seconds": 27.1936, "selection_time_seconds": 0.032, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 29901, 279, 4680, 323, 1379, 315, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 624, 17, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 264, 14452, 9315, 624, 18, 13, 663, 672, 279, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 44944, 476, 41274, 624, 19, 13, 14263, 279, 35067, 76960, 57685, 448, 12021, 11, 24353, 11, 323, 1008, 12685, 48559, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 51514, 35067, 76960, 57685, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 476, 926, 14725, 7215, 624, 21, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 1119, 279, 270, 