{"id": "641", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the key characteristics of red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs).\n- Compare and contrast these characteristics to highlight the differences and similarities.\n- Provide specific examples, numbers, or comparisons if mentioned in the passages.\n- Ensure that all details supporting the answer are included.\n- Do not add external information.\n- If the passages do not contain sufficient information, answer: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"\n- Output the answer after completing the analysis.\nThe key characteristics of red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) have been identified and compared. However, the passage does not provide specific examples, numbers, or comparisons to further elaborate on the differences and similarities. Therefore, I cannot provide detailed answers to the question based on the given information.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 27.838, "generation_time_seconds": 27.7899, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0376, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198