{"id": "40", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the sources of plastic in clothes dryer.\n2. Determine the type and extent of plastic contamination.\n3. Assess the effectiveness of current cleaning methods.\n4. Explore alternative cleaning methods that may be more effective.\n5. Evaluate the environmental impact of each method.\n6. Consider the cost-effectiveness and accessibility of the suggested methods.\n7. Select the most appropriate and feasible solution based on the above factors.\n8. Test the selected method(s) for effectiveness and practicality.\n8. Test the selected method(s) for effectiveness and practicality.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 10.289, "generation_time_seconds": 10.2518, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0313, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 8173, 315, 12188, 304, 15097, 46622, 624, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 943, 323, 12818, 315, 12188, 46710, 624, 18, 13, 81835, 279, 26279, 315, 1482, 15826, 5413, 624, 19, 13, 44052, 10555, 15826, 5413, 429, 1231, 