{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the relevant section of the Income Tax Act that deals with the treatment of assets discarded.\n2. Determine the specific provisions or rules for the disposal of assets as stated in the Income Tax Act.\n3. Check for any exceptions or special cases that may apply to the treatment of asset disposal.\n4. Consider the accounting implications of the treatment for the disposal of assets as per the Income Tax Act.\n5. Evaluate the tax implications for the disposal of assets under the Income Tax Act.\n6. Provide a comprehensive summary of the treatment for asset disposal as per the Income Tax Act, ensuring to include any relevant examples, numbers, or\n6. Provide a comprehensive summary of the treatment for asset disposal as per the Income Tax Act, ensuring to include any relevant examples, numbers, or comparisons if mentioned.\n- Identify the relevant section of the Income Tax Act that deals with the treatment of assets discarded.\n- Determine the specific provisions or rules for the disposal of assets as stated in the Income Tax Act.\n- Check for any exceptions or special cases that may apply to the treatment of asset disposal.\n- Consider the accounting implications of the treatment for the disposal of assets as per the Income Tax Act.\n- Evaluate the tax implications for the disposal of assets under the Income Tax Act.\n- Provide a comprehensive summary of the treatment for asset disposal as per the Income Tax Act, ensuring to include any relevant examples, numbers, or comparisons if mentioned.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 15.961, "generation_time_seconds": 15.8974, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0547, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 3151, 3772, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 429, 12506, 448, 279, 6380, 315, 11770, 979, 807, 525, 43210, 624, 17, 13, 37427, 2986, 279, 19156, 8826, 279, 33445, 315, 11770, 369, 3742, 9895, 624, 18, 13, 29901, 421, 1052, 525, 894, 3281, 5601, 476, 19585, 369, 3654, 4494, 315, 11770, 476, 14740, 624, 19, 13, 21144, 894, 29986, 476, 5107, 3742, 24154, 5815, 448, 279, 33445, 315, 11770, 624, 20, 13, 8116, 5612, 551, 279, 6380, 369, 9329, 33445, 438, 32640, 304, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.5203, -0.0001, -0.2117, -0.0035, -0.6854, -1.3427, -0.2117, -0.0, -0.0293, -0.0, -0