{"id": "195", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo attach multiple picture frames together, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n5. Repeat the process for additional frames, ensuring that the hinge placement is consistent across all frames.\n6. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang them up.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: Select frames with the same wood molding, lay them together, mark hinge placement, attach hinges, and attach a hanging wire to the back.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the types of picture frames you have available.\n2. Determine the size of the picture frames you want to attach.\n3. Consider the design and style of the picture frames you have.\n4. Decide on the type of attachment method you want to use (e.g., adhesive, screws, or brackets).\n5. Gather the necessary materials for the attachment method you have chosen.\n6. Prepare the surfaces where you want to attach the picture frames.\n7. Apply the attachment method to the picture frames.\n8. Attach the picture frames to the surfaces.\n9. Ensure the frames are level and straight after attachment.\n10. Allow any adhesive to dry completely or use screws and brackets securely if applicable.\n11. If using adhesive, consider applying a protective layer to prevent damage to the frames or surrounding surfaces.\n12. Clean up and dispose of any leftover materials or packaging.\n13. Test the stability of the attached picture frames by gently shaking or pushing on them to ensure they are securely fastened.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the types of picture frames you have available.\nStep 2: Determine the size of the picture frames you want to attach.\nStep 3: Consider the design and style of the picture frames you have.\nStep 4: Decide on the type of attachment method you want to use (e.g., adhesive, screws, or brackets).\nStep 5: Gather the necessary materials for the attachment method you have chosen.\nStep 6: Prepare the surfaces where you want to attach the picture frames.\nStep 7: Apply the attachment method to the picture frames.\nStep 8: Attach the picture frames to the\nStep 9: Ensure the frames are level and straight after attachment.\nStep 10: Allow any adhesive to dry completely or use screws and brackets securely if applicable.\nStep 11: If using adhesive, consider applying a protective layer to prevent damage to the frames or surrounding surfaces.\nStep 12: Clean up and dispose of any leftover materials or packaging.\nStep 13: Test the stability of the attached picture frames by gently shaking or pushing on them to ensure they are securely fastened.\n\nAnswer: To attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the types of picture frames you have available.\n2. Determine the size of the picture frames you want to attach.\n3. Consider the design and style of the picture frames you have.\n4. Decide on the type of attachment method you want to use (e.g., adhesive, screws, or brackets).\n5. Gather the necessary materials for the attachment method you have chosen.\n6. Prepare the surfaces where you want to attach the picture frames.\n7. Apply the attachment method to the picture frames.\n8. Attach the picture frames to the surfaces.\n9. Ensure the frames are level and straight after attachment.\n10. Allow any adhesive to dry completely or use screws and brackets securely if applicable.\n11. If using adhesive, consider applying a protective layer to prevent damage to the frames or surrounding surfaces.\n12. Clean up and dispose of any leftover materials or packaging.\n13. Test the stability of the attached picture frames by gently shaking or pushing on them to ensure they are securely fastened.", "time_sec": 23.916, "generation_time_seconds": 23.85, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0557, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.7229, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.0004, -23.6458, -18.4393, -2.8335, -2.4537, -7.8678, -7.5684, -9.6124, -7.9411, -6.9195, -6.1406, -6.2956, -6.5495, -4.1272, -1.5532, -1.3707, -4.0118, -5.9006, -5.4854, -5.4997, -4.4517, -4.2344, -3.8507, -5.2147, -5.0188, -4.5634, -4.4552, -6.32, -5.