{"id": "290", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Defrost the pork loin if possible. If you don't have time to defrost, you can place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour.\n2. Preheat the oven to 325°F (passage 2).\n3. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with 2 tsp of olive oil and season the outside with salt, pepper, and desired herbs (thyme, oregano, or garlic work well) (passage 2).\n4. Place the pork loin in a roasting pan and put it in the preheated oven (passage 2).\n5. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, or until the internal temperature reaches 150°F (passage 3).\n6. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature of the meat (passage 3).\n7. Once the meat is cooked, remove it from the oven and cover it with aluminum foil for 30 minutes before serving (passage 3).\n\nNote that the exact cooking time may vary depending on the size of the roast, so adjust the cooking time accordingly. Also, make sure to check the internal temperature of the meat to ensure that it is cooked all the way through.", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, first thaw the roast in the refrigerator for at least 24 hours for every 4 pounds of meat. Place the roast in a shallow tray or container to prevent it from dripping onto other food items. Once thawed, proceed with the cooking instructions provided in the recipe.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, first thaw the roast in the refrigerator for at least 24 hours for every 4 pounds of meat. Place the roast in a shallow tray or container to prevent it from dripping onto other food items. Once thawed, proceed with the cooking instructions provided in the recipe.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the frozen pork loin roast: The passage specifies that the pork loin roast is frozen, which means it needs to be thawed before cooking.\n2. Determine the thawing method: The passage does not specify a thawing method, so we cannot infer this from the given information. Common methods include thawing in the refrigerator (24 hours for each 4 pounds of meat) or using a microwave, but the passage does not provide details on this.\n3. Thawing in the refrigerator: If using the refrigerator method, ensure the roast is placed in a shallow tray or container to prevent it from dripping onto other food items. Allow the roast to thaw in the refrigerator for at least 24 hours for every 4 pounds of meat. For example, if you have an 8-pound pork loin roast, it would need to thaw for at least 48 hours.\n\nAnswer: To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, first thaw the roast in the refrigerator for at least 24 hours for every 4 pounds of meat. Place the roast in a shallow tray or container to prevent it from dripping onto other food items. Once thawed, proceed with the cooking instructions provided in the recipe.", "time_sec": 14.044, "generation_time_seconds": 14.0075, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0306, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 3151, 17233, 1714, 25, 576, 3405, 17064, 1246, 311, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.3243, -0.0003, -0.2467, -0.0019, -3.9597, -0.8278, -0.0077, -0.1755, -0.1002, -0.0895, -0.0211, -1.3966, -0.0, -0.0, -0.003, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0002, 0.0, -3.5776, -Infinity, -Infinity, -20.0236, -10.7347, -15.4167, -0.0137, -8.7093, -9.6808], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 147, "output_tokens": 32}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 15164