{"id": "358", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is that ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. On the other hand, poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, specifically attacking a person's integrity or intelligence to redirect the discussion towards their faults.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 6.917, "generation_time_seconds": 6.8777, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0327, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.7606, -0.0085, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.277, -8.4598, -15.8567, -10.6255, -8.9585], "cumulative_logprob": -44.9475, "norm_logp": -4.4947, "input_len": 153, "output_tokens": 10}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.7606, -0.0085, -0.0007, -0.0002, -0.277, -8.4598, -15.8567, -10.6255, -8.9585], "cumulative_logprob": -44.9475, "norm_logp": -4.4947, "input_len": 153, "output_tokens": 10}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 2, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.7606, -0.0085, -0.0007, -0.0002, -1.943