lative_logprob": -2.1313, "norm_logp": -0.2131, "input_len": 170, "output_tokens": 10}], "completions": [{"keep_idx": 3, "parent_beam": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16141, 25, 41444, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0002, -0.0948, -0.0473, -0.0112, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0052, -0.0014], "cumulative_logprob": -0.1604, "norm_logp": -0.0134, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 12}]}], "final": {"token_ids": [198, 16141, 25, 41444, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0652, -0.7158, -0.0364, -0.0148, -0.0, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.0, -0.0061, -0.0014], "cumulative_logprob": -0.8414, "norm_logp": -0.0701, "input_len": 136, "output_tokens": 12}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "508", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "pred": "Sirloin steak and porterhouse steak are both cuts of beef, but they differ in size, shape, and composition. A sirloin steak is a smaller, more tender cut of beef, typically from the lower back of the cow. It is known for its lean, tender meat and is often used for grilling or pan-searing. On the other hand, a porterhouse steak is a larger cut of beef, typically from the top of the cow. It is known for its marbling, which gives it a rich, flavorful taste. Porterhouse steaks are often used for grilling or pan-searing as well, but they are also popular for slicing into smaller steaks for serving. In summary, the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their size and composition, with sirloin being smaller and leaner, and porterhouse being larger and more marbled. Answer:[your answer here]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Sirloin steak and porterhouse steak are both cuts of beef, but they differ in size, shape, and composition. A sirloin steak is a smaller, more tender cut of beef, typically from the lower back of the cow. It is known for its lean, tender meat and is often used for grilling or pan-searing. On the other hand, a porterhouse steak is a larger cut of beef, typically from the top of the cow. It is known for its marbling, which gives it a rich, flavorful taste. Porterhouse steaks are often used for grilling or pan-searing as well, but they are also popular for slicing into smaller steaks for serving. In summary, the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their size and composition, with sirloin being smaller and leaner, and porterhouse being larger and more marbled. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the types of steaks mentioned: sirloin steak and porterhouse steak.\n2. Research the physical characteristics of each type of steak to understand the differences between them.\n3. Compare the size, shape, and composition of sirloin steak and porterhouse steak.\n4. Explore any additional details that might explain why these steaks are different, such as marbling or tenderness.\n5. Formulate an answer based on the research and comparison of the two steaks.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n5. Formulate an answer based on the research and comparison of the two steaks.\n\nAnswer: Sirloin steak and porterhouse steak are both cuts of beef, but they differ in size, shape, and composition. A sirloin steak is a smaller, more tender cut of beef, typically from the lower back of the cow. It is known for its lean, tender meat and is often used for grilling or pan-searing. On the other hand, a porterhouse steak is a larger cut of beef, typically from the top of the cow. It is known for its marbling, which gives it a rich, flavorful taste. Porterhouse steaks are often used for grilling or pan-searing as well, but they are also popular for slicing into smaller steaks for serving. In summary, the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their size and composition, with sirloin being smaller and leaner, and porterhouse being larger and more marbled. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 33.287, "generation_time_seconds": 33.2173, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0408, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198