{"id": "60", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to keep birds from building a nest on your porch is:\n\nAttach bird netting to the eaves or install bird netting over the light fixture, and/or mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "pred": "To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can try several methods. One effective approach is to use netting, which can be placed over the porch to prevent birds from accessing the area. Another option is to use spray deterrents, which can be applied to the porch to make it less appealing to birds. Additionally, you can consider installing birdhouses or other structures that provide alternative nesting sites, thereby reducing the likelihood of birds choosing your porch. It's also important to maintain the cleanliness and accessibility of the porch, as birds may be deterred by a cluttered or uninviting space. Finally, understanding the specific type of birds that are most likely to build nests on your porch can help tailor the deterrent methods more effectively. By implementing a combination of these strategies, you can significantly reduce the chances of birds choosing your porch as a nesting site. Answer:[your answer here]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can try several methods. One effective approach is to use netting, which can be placed over the porch to prevent birds from accessing the area. Another option is to use spray deterrents, which can be applied to the porch to make it less appealing to birds. Additionally, you can consider installing birdhouses or other structures that provide alternative nesting sites, thereby reducing the likelihood of birds choosing your porch. It's also important to maintain the cleanliness and accessibility of the porch, as birds may be deterred by a cluttered or uninviting space. Finally, understanding the specific type of birds that are most likely to build nests on your porch can help tailor the deterrent methods more effectively. By implementing a combination of these strategies, you can significantly reduce the chances of birds choosing your porch as a nesting site. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the specific problem: The problem is about preventing birds from building nests on a porch.\n2. Analyze the given information: The question does not provide any specific details about the type of birds, the condition of the porch, or previous experiences with bird nests.\n3. Consider possible solutions: Based on common knowledge, one might consider methods to deter birds such as using netting, spraying, or other deterrents.\n4. Evaluate the effectiveness of the solutions: The effectiveness of these methods can vary depending on the specific circumstances, such as the type of birds, the size of the porch, and the persistence of the birds\nThe reasoning steps are:\n5. Research specific deterrents: Investigate the effectiveness of netting, spray deterrents, and other methods by looking for scientific studies or reviews that evaluate their success rates and long-term impact.\n6. Consider the physical condition of the porch: Assess the condition of the porch, including cleanliness, accessibility, and any potential hiding spots for birds to build nests.\n7. Evaluate the type of birds: Determine the species of birds that are most likely to build nests on the porch to tailor the deterrent methods appropriately.\n8. Check for previous experiences: Review any past experiences with bird nests on the porch to understand the behavior and persistence of the\n\nAnswer: To keep birds from building a nest on your porch, you can try several methods. One effective approach is to use netting, which can be placed over the porch to prevent birds from accessing the area. Another option is to use spray deterrents, which can be applied to the porch to make it less appealing to birds. Additionally, you can consider installing birdhouses or other structures that provide alternative nesting sites, thereby reducing the likelihood of birds choosing your porch. It's also important to maintain the cleanliness and accessibility of the porch, as birds may be deterred by a cluttered or uninviting space. Finally, understanding the specific type of birds that are most likely to build nests on your porch can help tailor the deterrent methods more effectively. By implementing a combination of these strategies, you can significantly reduce the chances of birds choosing your porch as a nesting site. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 20.768, "generation_time_seconds": 20.7288, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0321, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 3151, 3491, 25, 576, 3491, 374, 911, 26160, 19654, 504, 4752, 95121, 389, 264, 44647, 624, 17, 13, 37427, 2986, 279, 2661, 1995, 25, 576, 3405, 1558, 537, 3410, 894, 3151, 3565, 911, 279, 943, 315, 19654, 11, 279, 2971, 315, 279, 44647, 11, 476, 3681, 11449, 448, 11958, 95121, 624, 18, 13, 21144, 3204, 9904, 25, 20205, 389, 4185, 6540, 11, 825, 2578, 2908, 5413, 311, 4040, 19654, 1741, 438, 1667, 4179, 1280, 11, 82536, 11, 476, 1008, 82620, 82, 624, 19, 13, 54115, 279, 26279, 315, 279, 9904, 25, 576, 26279, 315, 1493, 5413, 646, 13289, 11649, 389, 279, 3151, 13161, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 943, 315, 19654, 11, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 44647, 11, 323, 279, 40956, 315, 279, 196