{"id": "85", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end. Then, take another clean slide and holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry and label clearly. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers. Always avoid coming into contact with another person's blood and if it is unavoidable, wear rubber gloves.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of blood sample needed for the slide preparation.\n2. Ensure the sample is fresh and uncontaminated.\n3. Prepare the slide with a clean, sterile glass slide and cover slip.\n4. Place a drop of blood on the slide, making sure not to exceed the capacity of the slide's surface area.\n5. Gently spread the blood sample across the slide using a disposable slide spreader or a clean, sterile toothpick.\n6. Allow the blood to settle for a short period to ensure even distribution.\n7. Cover the blood sample with the cover slip, ensuring it is properly aligned and free of\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 15.13, "generation_time_seconds": 15.09, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0327, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16250, 2685, 279, 2266, 323, 7428, 315, 279, 3405, 13, 576, 3405, 374, 10161, 369, 279, 1