{"id": "124", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4\" and set and level them according to the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the plans. Check for squareness and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Cut two more 4 x 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids and, when the frame is square, toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The size of the shed can be adjusted as needed.", "pred": "The next logical reasoning step after adding the doors and windows to the shed would be to ensure that all the structural components are properly aligned and secured. This includes checking that the walls are plumb (vertically straight), the roof is pitched correctly, and all joints are tight and secure. Additionally, it would be important to inspect the stability of the shed, ensuring that it is structurally sound and can withstand environmental factors such as wind and rain. This step is crucial to ensure the long-term durability and safety of the shed.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The next logical reasoning step after adding the doors and windows to the shed would be to ensure that all the structural components are properly aligned and secured. This includes checking that the walls are plumb (vertically straight), the roof is pitched correctly, and all joints are tight and secure. Additionally, it would be important to inspect the stability of the shed, ensuring that it is structurally sound and can withstand environmental factors such as wind and rain. This step is crucial to ensure the long-term durability and safety of the shed.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Begin by gathering materials including wood, nails, a hammer, and saw.\n2. Measure and cut the wood to appropriate lengths, ensuring that you have enough to build the shed's walls and roof.\n3. Assemble the walls by attaching the sides to the front and back pieces of wood.\n4. Construct the roof by attaching the roof pieces to the wall pieces, ensuring they are securely fastened.\n5. Add the roof to the shed, making sure it is properly aligned and secured.\n6. Add the doors and windows to the shed.\n7. Add any finishing touches such as paint or sealant to the shed\nThe next logical reasoning step after adding the doors and windows to the shed would be to ensure that all the structural components are properly aligned and secured. This includes checking that the walls are plumb (vertically straight), the roof is pitched correctly, and all joints are tight and secure. Additionally, it would be important to inspect the stability of the shed, ensuring that it is structurally sound and can withstand environmental factors such as wind and rain. This step is crucial to ensure the long-term durability and safety of the shed.\nAnswer: The next logical reasoning step after adding the doors and windows to the shed would be to ensure that all the structural components are properly aligned and secured. This includes checking that the walls are plumb (vertically straight), the roof is pitched correctly, and all joints are tight and secure. Additionally, it would be important to inspect the stability of the shed, ensuring that it is structurally sound and can withstand environmental factors such as wind and rain. This step is crucial to ensure the long-term durability and safety of the shed.\n\nAnswer: The next logical reasoning step after adding the doors and windows to the shed would be to ensure that all the structural components are properly aligned and secured. This includes checking that the walls are plumb (vertically straight), the roof is pitched correctly, and all joints are tight and secure. Additionally, it would be important to inspect the stability of the shed, ensuring that it is structurally sound and can withstand environmental factors such as wind and rain. This step is crucial to ensure the long-term durability and safety of the shed.", "time_sec": 24.12, "generation_time_seconds": 24.0823, "selection_time_seconds": 0.029, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 510, 16, 13, 70894, 279, 6770, 5944, 315, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 624, 17, 13, 48995, 7236, 4362, 369, 279, 8086, 624, 18, 13, 34104, 323, 10549, 279, 2747, 624, 19, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 24354, 594, 4034, 624, 20, 13, 19242, 279, 65425, 3684, 624, 21, 13, 48384, 75685, 311, 279, 24354, 624, 22, 13, 19242, 264, 6006, 323, 11030, 624, 23, 13, 2691, 264, 16266, 323, 41523, 624, 24, 13, 18608, 279, 24354, 553, 7842, 894, 5107, 4419, 476, 24284, 28627, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.4876, -0.012, -0.0003, -0.0001, -2.8759, -0.0018, -0.0001, -2.5535, -0.0009, -2.3366, -0.1656, -0.084, -0.0036, -0.0016, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0648, -0.0013, 0.0, -0.7529, -0.9718, -1.0923, -0.0272, -1.7021, -0.335, -0.0663, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.9352, -0.2519, -1.0077, -0.0001, -0.4659, -0.023, -0.0002, 0.0, -1.4821, 0.0, -0.0016, -2.3137, -1.6179, -0.1915, -0.0076, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2327, -0.0124, -1.4507, -1.1643, -0.0002, -0.0001, 0.0, -1.8993, -1.2024, -3.1272, -0.0007, -0.2112, -0.2055, -0.0001, 0.0, -1.2575, -0.6415, -0.0302, -0.0293, -0.1656, -0.0909, -0.0001, 0