{"id": "135", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Here are brief answers to the question on how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nPassage 1: The passage does not provide information on how to roast individual garlic cloves specifically. However, it does mention that larger garlic cloves may take up to an hour to soften when roasted, so it is possible to assume that smaller cloves will take less time.\n\nPassage 2: This passage provides some options for seasoning the garlic before roasting, but it does not provide instructions on how to roast individual garlic cloves.\n\nPassage 3: This passage provides a method for roasting entire garlic heads, but it does not address how to roast individual garlic cloves. The passage does mention that cutting the top of the garlic bulb and exposing the individual cloves can help them roast more evenly, but it does not provide specific instructions on how to do this.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "roast garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-30 minutes, depending on the size and desired level of roast.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: roast garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-30 minutes, depending on the size and desired level of roast.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the garlic cloves to be roasted.\n2. Preheat the oven to a suitable temperature, typically between 375°F and 400°F (190°C to 200°C).\n3. Place the garlic cloves on a baking sheet or a roasting pan.\n4. Drizzle the garlic cloves with olive oil or any preferred cooking oil.\n5. Season the garlic cloves with salt, pepper, and any other desired seasonings.\n6. Roast the garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-30 minutes, depending on the size and desired level of\nRoast the garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-30 minutes, depending on the size and desired level of\nAnswer: roast garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-30 minutes, depending on the size and desired level of roast.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: roast garlic cloves in the preheated oven for about 20-30 minutes, depending on the size and desired level of roast.", "time_sec": 24.786, "generation_time_seconds": 24.7231, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0564, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 1714, 315, 926, 14725, 3842, 30635, 84288, 624, 17, 13, 48995, 279, 5871, 7375, 323, 13966, 624, 18, 13, 31166, 279, 30635, 84288, 369, 926, 14725, 624, 19, 13, 11830, 559, 279, 30635, 84288, 304, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 4248, 279, 30635, 84288, 369, 1513, 23709, 624, 21, 13, 26530, 279, 53562, 30635, 311, 7010, 323, 8651, 279, 84288, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.0785, -0.0002, -0.1163, -0.0023, -1.728, -0.5264, -0.0053, 0.0, -0.511, -0.0, -0.0, -0.1845, -0.0163, 0.0, -1.3336, -0.7148, -0.0161, -0.7349, -0.0241, -0.0031, -0.0792, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0711, -0.0005, -0.0002, -0.0003, -0.3679, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0063, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0218, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0008, -0.0, -1.203, -0.2858, -0.0533, -0.5176, -0.0, 0.0, -0.5507, -0.3088, -0.3715, -0.0001, -0.0043, -0.0175, 0.0, -0.026, -0.0002, 0.0, -3.4094, -0.0002, -3.1681, -0.0002, -1.5019, -0.0, -2.8028, -0.263, -0.1074, -0.0046, -1.561, -0.2195, -Infinity, -12.7515, -10.2084, -13.3333, -15.9375, -6.5394, -11.919, -8.