{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Excel sheet you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Click on the \"Data\" tab on the Ribbon at the top of the Excel window.\n3. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button.\n4. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, under the \"Column\" dropdown menu, select the column you want to sort alphabetically.\n5. Under the \"Order\" dropdown menu, select \"A to Z\" or \"Ascending\" if you want the column to be sorted from the beginning of the alphabet to the end.\n6. Click \"OK\" to sort the selected column alphabetically.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Open the Excel sheet you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Click on the \"Data\" tab on the Ribbon at the top of the Excel window.\n3. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button.\n4. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, under the \"Column\" dropdown menu, select the column you want to sort alphabetically.\n5. Under the \"Order\" dropdown menu, select \"A to Z\" or \"Ascending\" if you want the column to be sorted from the beginning of the alphabet to the end.\n6. Click \"OK\" to sort the\nThe reasoning steps are:\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Excel sheet you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Click on the \"Data\" tab on the Ribbon at the top of the Excel window.\n3. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button.\n4. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, under the \"Column\" dropdown menu, select the column you want to sort alphabetically.\n5. Under the \"Order\" dropdown menu, select \"A to Z\" or \"Ascending\" if you want the column to be sorted from the beginning of the alphabet to the end.\n6. Click \"OK\" to sort the selected column alphabetically.", "time_sec": 29.93, "generation_time_seconds": 29.8689, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0518, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 9760, 1995, 911, 76118, 458, 21029, 10834, 304, 83298, 1973, 304, 279, 2661, 21085, 1141, 4292, 17, 13, 29279, 429, 279, 21085, 5707, 2797, 11221, 476, 10295, 5435, 311, 28273, 821, 27790, 2673, 304, 21029, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 14016, 1995, 11, 31094, 448, 330, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 1189, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.9884, -0.0001, -0.1625, -0.0006, -3.6032, -0.1015, -3.127, -0.0132, -0.0082, -0.0055, -0.0, -5.6289, -0.0012, -0.0, -2.9951, -0.0, -0.0363, -1.3445, -2.5034, -0.1758, -0.0036, 0.0, -3.5693, -0.3699, -0.0521, -0.6186, -3.1838, -0.8444, -0.0548, -0.0341, -0.8146, -4.2771, 0.0, -0.174, -0.0892, -0.0968, 0.0, -0.1938