{"id": "431", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first determine the extent of the tarnish. If the jewelry is slightly dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth into the solution. Rub the jewelry with the cloth, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the jewelry and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can also try submerging it in a hot saltwater bath. Ensure that if your jewelry has gemstones, they won't be affected by the saltwater. For diamonds, clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, and pat dry with a soft cloth.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of metal in the jewelry (e.g., silver, gold, platinum).\n2. Determine the type of tarnish (e.g., sulfuric tarnish, oxidation).\n3. Choose an appropriate cleaning method based on the type of metal and tarnish. For example, silver jewelry can be cleaned with a mixture of vinegar and water, while gold jewelry may require a different approach.\n4. Prepare the cleaning solution or agent (e.g., vinegar, baking soda, or commercial jewelry cleaner). For silver, a mixture of equal parts vinegar and water can be used. For gold, a solution of baking soda and water may be more appropriate.\n5. Apply the cleaning solution or agent to the jewelry. For silver, dip the jewelry in the vinegar and water mixture. For gold, use a soft brush to apply the baking soda and water solution.\n6. Let the jewelry sit in the solution for a specified time (e.g., 10-20 minutes). For silver, this time can be shorter, while for gold, it may need to be longer.\n7. Rinse the jewelry thoroughly with clean water. For silver, use a clean cloth to dry the jewelry. For gold, use a soft, dry cloth to avoid scratching the surface.\n8. Store the jewelry in a dry, acid-free environment to prevent further tarnishing. For silver, use a silver polish to maintain the shine. For gold, use a gold polish to keep the surface smooth and lustrous. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the type of metal in the jewelry (e.g., silver, gold, platinum).\n2. Determine the type of tarnish (e.g., sulfuric tarnish, oxidation).\n3. Choose an appropriate cleaning method based on the type of metal and tarnish.\n4. Prepare the cleaning solution or agent (e.g., vinegar, baking soda, or commercial jewelry cleaner).\n5. Apply the cleaning solution or agent to the jewelry.\n6. Let the jewelry sit in the solution for a specified time (e.g., 10-20 minutes).\n7. Rinse the jewelry thoroughly with clean water.\n8\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of metal in the jewelry (e.g., silver, gold, platinum).\n2. Determine the type of tarnish (e.g., sulfuric tarnish, oxidation).\n3. Choose an appropriate cleaning method based on the type of metal and tarnish. For example, silver jewelry can be cleaned with a mixture of vinegar and water, while gold jewelry may require a different approach.\n4. Prepare the cleaning solution or agent (e.g., vinegar, baking soda, or commercial jewelry cleaner). For silver, a mixture of equal parts vinegar and water can be used. For gold, a solution of baking soda and water may be more appropriate.\n5. Apply the cleaning solution or agent to the jewelry. For silver, dip the jewelry in the vinegar and water mixture. For gold, use a soft brush to apply the baking soda and water solution.\n6. Let the jewelry sit in the solution for a specified time (e.g., 10-20 minutes). For silver, this time can be shorter, while for gold, it may need to be longer.\n7. Rinse the jewelry thoroughly with clean water. For silver, use a clean cloth to dry the jewelry. For gold, use a soft, dry cloth to avoid scratching the surface.\n8. Store the jewelry in a dry, acid-free environment to prevent further tarnishing. For silver, use a silver polish to maintain the shine. For gold, use a gold polish to keep the surface smooth and lustrous. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 46.368, "generation_time_seconds": 46.3231, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0372, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.7608, -0.0115, -0.0003, -0.0, -0.152, -8.5519, -14.8202, -12.5001, -6.5773, -10.1053, -5.3243, -4.5066, -5.6821, -4.255, -1.2909, -1.2006, -1.4075, -1.2986, -1.1986, -0.3515, -0.4689, -0.288, -0.3851, -2.0993, -2.6104, -2.0336, -1.5126, -0.30