{"id": "644", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, first cut large potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, being careful not to break the long sprouts. Place these chunks on a tray and let them dry out in a cool, dark place overnight. Small, sprouted potatoes can be planted whole. Next, prepare your planting area by turning the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches, removing any large rocks or debris. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. Cut your potatoes into cubes of about 1 to 2 inches, making sure to leave a sprout on each cube. Place these cubes in the trench, sprouted side facing up, spaced about 6 to 8 inches apart. Cover the potatoes with compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. Water the potatoes thoroughly and regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Finally, add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, keeping it at least 4 inches away from the sprouting potato vines. This mulch will help keep the soil cool and maintain a consistent moisture level.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the sprouted potato.\n2. Choose a suitable planting location.\n3. Prepare the soil for planting.\n4. Dig a hole for the potato.\n5. Plant the sprouted potato in the hole.\n6. Cover the potato with soil.\n7. Water the planted potato.\n8. Maintain the potato plant with regular watering and care.\n9. Monitor the potato plant for growth and harvest when ready.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 17.848, "generation_time_seconds": 17.8031, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0357, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0