{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of blood slide preparation method being asked about. Is it a wet mount, a stained slide, or another type?\n2. Determine if there are specific steps or techniques mentioned in the passages for the type of blood slide preparation being asked about.\n3. If the passages do not provide sufficient information, recognize that the question cannot be answered based on the given data.\n4. If sufficient information is provided in the passages, list the steps or techniques for preparing the blood slide.\n5. Provide examples, numbers, or comparisons if mentioned in the passages.\n6. Include all details that support the answer.\n7. Ensure\nThe reasoning steps are:\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 19.994, "generation_time_seconds": 19.9495, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0375, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 6543, 14983, 17975, 1714, 1660, 13862, 311, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 15392, 336, 9081, 51964, 11, 26741, 12010, 26862, 9081, 51964, 11, 4992, 13, 4292, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 3151, 7354, 323, 7236, 436