{"id": "125", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "pred": "The next logical step after gathering the necessary tools and equipment is to start by constructing the foundation or base of the shed. This step is crucial as it provides a stable and secure base for the entire structure. The foundation can be made from various materials depending on the type of shed and the local conditions, such as concrete, gravel, or even wood. Ensuring that the foundation is properly level and stable is essential for the overall stability and longevity of the shed. Once the foundation is complete, the next step would be to assemble the frame of the shed using the chosen materials, which will provide the structure for the walls, roof, and other components of the shed.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The next logical step after gathering the necessary tools and equipment is to start by constructing the foundation or base of the shed. This step is crucial as it provides a stable and secure base for the entire structure. The foundation can be made from various materials depending on the type of shed and the local conditions, such as concrete, gravel, or even wood. Ensuring that the foundation is properly level and stable is essential for the overall stability and longevity of the shed. Once the foundation is complete, the next step would be to assemble the frame of the shed using the chosen materials, which will provide the structure for the walls, roof, and other components of the shed.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the materials needed for the lean-to shed.\n- Measure the space available for the shed.\n- Determine the dimensions of the shed.\n- Choose the orientation and location of the shed.\n- Design the structure, including the roof, walls, and floor.\n- Gather the necessary tools and equipment for construction.\n- Start by constructing the foundation or base of the shed.\n- Assemble the frame of the shed using the chosen materials.\n- Construct the walls and roof using the frame.\n- Install the doors and windows, if required.\n- Add any finishing touches, such as paint or weatherproofing.\n- Ensure the shed is level\nThe next logical step in building a lean-to shed is to gather the necessary tools and equipment for construction.\nThe next logical step after gathering the necessary tools and equipment is to start by constructing the foundation or base of the shed. This step is crucial as it provides a stable and secure base for the entire structure. The foundation can be made from various materials depending on the type of shed and the local conditions, such as concrete, gravel, or even wood. Ensuring that the foundation is properly level and stable is essential for the overall stability and longevity of the shed. Once the foundation is complete, the next step would be to assemble the frame of the shed using the chosen materials, which will provide the structure for the walls, roof, and\n\nAnswer: The next logical step after gathering the necessary tools and equipment is to start by constructing the foundation or base of the shed. This step is crucial as it provides a stable and secure base for the entire structure. The foundation can be made from various materials depending on the type of shed and the local conditions, such as concrete, gravel, or even wood. Ensuring that the foundation is properly level and stable is essential for the overall stability and longevity of the shed. Once the foundation is complete, the next step would be to assemble the frame of the shed using the chosen materials, which will provide the structure for the walls, roof, and other components of the shed.", "time_sec": 19.248, "generation_time_seconds": 19.207, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0349, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 70894, 279, 7428, 315, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 624, 17, 13, 48995, 7236, 323, 7375, 4362, 369, 8086, 624, 18, 13, 34104, 323, 1868, 279, 3082, 369, 279, 24354, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 279, 16266, 476, 4910, 369, 279, 24354, 624, 20, 13, 18678, 279, 2331, 476, 6422, 315, 279, 24354, 624, 21, 13, 7854, 279, 14285, 315, 279, 24354, 624, 22, 13, 19242, 279, 15134, 315, 279, 24354, 624, 23, 13, 2691, 894, 5871, 4419, 1075, 264, 6006, 476, 11030, 624, 24, 13, 35533, 279, 24354, 594, 27263, 624, 16, 15, 13, 19242, 894, 24284, 28627, 1075, 264, 89051, 476, 17716, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.3834, -0.0003, -2.767, -0.0012, -0.4669, -0.9257, -0.4331, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0004, -1.3856, -0.0171, 0.0, -0.6793, -0.523, -0.4736, -0.0002, -0.1793, -0.1268, -0.1659, -0.01, -0.0011, 0.0, -0.9057, -0.2092, -0.6154, -0.0003, -0.4449, -0.5103, -0.0651, -0.0114, -0.1083, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.9083, -0.0056, -0.0963, -1.9488, -0.279, -0.6645, -0.111, -0.001, -0.0683, -0.0007, 0.0, -0.5901, -0.0, -1.4469, -1.3049, -0.1724, -0.0264, 0.0, -0.0067, -0.0024, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.5233, -0.0002, -0.1888, -0.0405, 0.0, -0.3022, -0.1361, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.2372, -0.0049, -0.0178, -0.3589, 0.0, -0.0036, -0.0013, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1275, -0.1636, -0.5835, -0.8418, -1.5264, -3.6461, -0.0019, -0.1836, -0.0805, -0.0011, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.6217, -0.0574, -0.6856, -4.4867, -0.1181, -2.4533, -0.0004, 0.0, 0.0, -0.7441, -0.2388, -1.4596, -0.0024, -2.832, -0.5398, -2.0818, -0.0199, -1.8502, -0.6371, -Infinity, -21.3