ens": 10}]}], "final": {"token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0353, -0.27, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0025, -0.0001, -0.0108, -0.0572], "cumulative_logprob": -0.3761, "norm_logp": -0.0376, "input_len": 374, "output_tokens": 10}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.94, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "146", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sew a zipper gusset:\n\n1. Make a casing in the side seams by stitching the outer edge of the gusset and the back side seam.\n2. Slide the boning right down into the casing.\n3. Push the seam allowance to the back and tack the casing to the lining, if necessary, so it doesn't move.\n4. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\n5. Sew across the top of the zipper sandwich with a zipper foot, making sure to line up the three edges.\n6. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper.\n7. Trace all pattern pieces to the remaining fabric and cut them out.\n8. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, with the right sides facing each other, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n9. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the zipper gusset, with the right sides facing down, and stitch along the seam line.\n10. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n11. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n12. The width of the zipper between the gusset should measure 1/2\".\n13. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch along the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics together nicely.\n\nTherefore, to sew a zipper gusset, you need to make a casing in the side seams, insert the boning, make a zipper sandwich, sew the zipper gusset to the zipper, and attach the lining to the zipper gusset.", "pred": "To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the materials needed: fabric, zipper, and sewing tools (scissors, sewing machine, pins, etc.).\n2. Determine the size and shape of the zipper gusset based on the dimensions of the garment it will be attached to, ensuring it fits properly and provides the desired functionality.\n3. Prepare the fabric by cutting it to the desired shape and size according to the dimensions determined in step 2. Ensure the edges are straight and the fabric is free of wrinkles.\n4. Attach the zipper to the fabric by following the manufacturer's instructions or using a zipper foot on a sewing machine to sew the zipper tape to the fabric.\n5. Insert the slider of the zipper into the teeth of the zipper tape, ensuring it is centered and aligned with the fabric.\n6. Continue sewing the zipper tape to the fabric, using a straight stitch to secure the zipper in place.\n7. Trim any excess fabric or zipper tape, ensuring the edges are neat and even. Use scissors to cut the fabric and zipper tape to the desired length.\n8. Finish the edges of the zipper gusset by overlocking or zigzag stitching to prevent fraying and ensure a neat appearance. Use a serger or a zigzag stitch on a sewing machine to create a clean finish.\n9. Press the fabric and zipper gusset to smooth out any wrinkles and ensure the edges are flat and even.\n10. Attach the zipper gusset to the garment by sewing it in place, ensuring it is centered and aligned with the other seams. Use a straight stitch or a zigzag stitch to secure the zipper gusset to the garment.\n11. Check the zipper gusset for proper functionality by opening and closing the zipper. Ensure it operates smoothly and without any resistance.\n12. If necessary, make any adjustments to the zipper gusset or the garment to ensure a proper fit and functionality. This may include trimming the fabric or adjusting the position of the zipper gusset.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n2. Identify the materials needed for sewing a zipper gusset, such as fabric, zipper, and sewing tools (scissors, sewing machine, pins, etc.).\n3. Determine the size and shape of the zipper gusset based on the dimensions of the garment it will be attached to, ensuring it fits properly and provides the desired functionality.\n4. Prepare the fabric by cutting it to the desired shape and size according to the dimensions determined in step 3. Ensure the edges are straight and the fabric is free of wrinkles.\n5. Attach the zipper to the fabric by following the manufacturer's instructions or using a zipper foot on a sewing machine to sew the zipper tape to the fabric.\n6. Insert the slider of the zipper into the teeth of the zipper tape, ensuring it is centered and aligned with the fabric.\n7. Continue sewing the zipper tape to the fabric, using a straight stitch to secure the zipper in place.\n8. Trim any excess fabric or zipper tape,\n\nAnswer: To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the materials needed: fabric, zipper, and sewing tools (scissors, sewing machine, pins, etc.).\n2. Determine the size and shape of the zipper gusset based on the dimensions of the garment it will be attached to, ensuring it fits properly and provides the desired functionality.\n3. Prepare the fabric by cutting it to the desired shape and size according to the dimensions determined in step 2. Ensure the edges are straight and the fabric is free of wrinkles.\n4. Attach the zipper to the fabric by following the manufacturer's instructions or using a zipper foot on a sewing machine to sew the zipper tape to the fabric.\n5. Insert the slider of the zipper into the teeth of the zipper tape, ensuring it is centered and aligned with the fabric.\n6. Continue sewing the zipper tape to the fabric, using a straight stitch to secure the zipper in place.\n7. Trim any excess fabric or zipper tape, ensuring the edges are neat and even. Use scissors to cut the fabric and zipper tape to the desired length.\n8. Finish the edges of the zipper gusset by overlocking or zigzag stitching to prevent fraying and ensure a neat appearance. Use a serger or a zigzag stitch on a sewing machine to create a clean finish.\n9. Press the fabric and zipper gusset to smooth out any wrinkles and ensure the edges are flat and even.\n10. Attach the zipper gusset to the garment by sewing it in place, ensuring it is centered and aligned with the other seams. Use a straight stitch or a zigzag stitch to secure the zipper gusset to the garment.\n11. Check the zipper gusset for proper functionality by opening and closing the zipper. Ensure it operates smoothly and without any resistance.\n12. If necessary, make any adjustments to the zipper gusset or the garment to ensure a proper fit and functionality. This may include trimming the fabric or adjusting the position of the zipper gusset.", "time_sec": 32.168, "generation_time_seconds": 32.1294, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0321, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.5994, -0.0075, -0.0002, -0.0, -2.4174, -Infinity, -14.5437, -11.4586, -9.8116, -10.9265, -6.1022, -6.2174, -6.5247, -5.4763, -2.2132, -2.3481, -3.6248, -3.0635, -1.2688, -0.7966, -1.265, -1.509, -2.1147, -2.4054, -2.301, -1.2831, -1.3773, -0.2639, -0.2639, -1.523, -2.7949, -5.6321, -7.0864, -4.3902], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 35}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 7236, 4362, 25, 29901, 1128, 7236, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 1855, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1741, 438, 13055, 11, 68761, 11, 4516, 11, 323, 51219, 5662, 382, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.5994, -0.0002, -0.2177, -0.0018, -0.545, -0.0969, -1.0814, -2.5005, -1.0744, -0.6674, -1.6953, -0.2746, -0.163, -0.925, -1.372, -0.3025, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, 