.2928, -0.6379, -0.3375, -0.7707, -0.4779, -0.6862, -0.0393, -0.1089, -0.7019, -1.569, -0.2359, -0.0324, -1.0438, -0.9694, -0.2563, -0.0212, -0.6535, -0.7773, -0.4102, -0.5301, -1.0139, -0.0306, -0.0632, -1.5805, -0.3216, -0.5697, -0.0001, -0.229, -0.2413, -0.0793, -0.0003, -0.3355, -0.0128, -0.0833, -0.0693, -1.198, -1.8836, -0.9151, -1.7361, -0.8134, -0.0971, -0.0647, -1.1198, -0.5837, -0.6246, -0.0036, -0.0023, -0.0193, -0.0084], "cumulative_logprob": -32.2224, "norm_logp": -0.4603, "input_len": 206, "output_tokens": 70}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "183", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "pred": "To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325°F (163°C). Place the roast in the oven and cook for about 20 minutes per pound, plus an additional 10 minutes per pound. For example, if the roast weighs 2 pounds, it would need to be cooked for approximately 60 minutes. Answer:[your answer here]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325°F (163°C). Place the roast in the oven and cook for about 20 minutes per pound, plus an additional 10 minutes per pound. For example, if the roast weighs 2 pounds, it would need to be cooked for approximately 60 minutes. Answer:[your answer here]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of meat and its size: The passage mentions a \"small prime rib roast.\" This indicates that the meat is a cut of beef, specifically the prime rib, and that it is small in size.\n2. Determine the cooking method: The passage specifies that the cooking method is to be done in the oven. This sets the context for the cooking process and the temperature and time required.\n3. Research the cooking time and temperature: To cook a prime rib roast in the oven, you need to know the appropriate temperature and cooking time. Typically, a small prime rib roast is cooked at around 325°F (163°C) for about 20 minutes per pound, plus an additional 10 minutes per pound. For example, if the roast weighs 2 pounds, it would need to be cooked for approximately 60 minutes.\n\nAnswer: To cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325°F (163°C). Place the roast in the oven and cook for about 20 minutes per pound, plus an additional 10 minutes per pound. For example, if the roast weighs 2 pounds, it would need to be cooked for approximately 60 minutes. Answer:[your answer here]", "time_sec": 26.716, "generation_time_seconds": 26.6771, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0325, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 12, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 23387, 25, 29901, 3425, 279, 23387, 374, 390, 79198, 476, 20692, 13, 1200, 79198, 297, 21097, 4225, 6334, 4017, 3720, 11, 892, 8609, 4296, 3607, 38292, 323, 803, 41047, 1091, 20692, 297, 21097, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -3.1891, -0.1873, -0.0051, -0.4993, -0.0189, -2.486, -0.9584, -0.8663, -0.4574, -0.0671, -0.0025, -0.0256, -3.0211, -0.0, -0.0675, -0.0141, -1.2897, -0.2526, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.4085, 0.0, -0.0384, -0.0, -0.7892, -0.288, -2.9948, -0.1416, -0.3912, -8.3919, -0.0032, -0.0063, -0.0011, -0.6114, -0.5261, -0.0, 0.0, -1.2992, -Infinity, -Infinity, -14.3777, -7.1888, -22.5, -14.1987], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 146, "output_tokens": 46}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-