{"id": "294", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "To properly fertilize your grass, you should fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for your specific grass type. For warm season grasses, this would be when the grass turns green in the early spring. You should also know the type of fertilizer to use based on the type of grass you have and do a pH soil test to ensure the fertilizer has the appropriate pH for your soil. Once you've determined the correct fertilizer and timing, apply it in a perpendicular pattern and check the lawn after application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape, but if it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "pred": "The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps: identifying the type of grass, determining the soil type, checking the soil pH, testing for nutrient deficiencies, choosing the appropriate fertilizer, and applying it according to the instructions.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps: identifying the type of grass, determining the soil type, checking the soil pH, testing for nutrient deficiencies, choosing the appropriate fertilizer, and applying it according to the instructions.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the type of grass you have in your lawn. Different grass types have different nutrient requirements.\n- Determine the soil type in your lawn. Soil type affects nutrient availability and root growth.\n- Check the soil pH. Most grasses prefer a pH between 6.0 and 7.0.\n- Test the soil for nutrient deficiencies. Common deficiencies include nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium.\n- Choose the appropriate fertilizer. For example, a slow-release fertilizer is better for long-term nutrient supply.\n- Apply fertilizer according to the instructions on the package. This typically involves spreading the fertilizer evenly over the lawn and watering it in.\nAnswer: The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps: identifying the type of grass, determining the soil type, checking the soil pH, testing for nutrient deficiencies, choosing the appropriate fertilizer, and applying it according to the instructions.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps: identifying the type of grass, determining the soil type, checking the soil pH, testing for nutrient deficiencies, choosing the appropriate fertilizer, and applying it according to the instructions.", "time_sec": 22.946, "generation_time_seconds": 22.9097, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0294, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 12, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 304, 697, 36025, 13, 33396, 16359, 4494, 614, 2155, 49023, 8502, 624, 12, 29901, 279, 17171, 943, 304, 697, 36025, 13, 75519, 943, 21501, 49023, 18048, 323, 3704, 6513, 624, 12, 4248, 279, 17171, 36043, 13, 7496, 16359, 288, 10702, 264, 36043, 1948, 220, 21, 13, 15, 323, 220, 22, 13, 15, 624, 12, 3393, 279, 17171, 369, 49023, 71846, 13, 7718, 71846, 2924, 46403, 11, 31988, 29869, 11, 323, 61175, 624, 12, 22201, 279, 8311, 64291, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 264, 6301, 44724, 64291, 374, 2664, 369, 1293, 9663, 49023, 8149, 624, 12, 20552, 64291, 4092, 311, 279, 11221, 389, 279, 6328, 13, 1096, 11136, 17601, 30035, 279, 64291, 41047, 916, 279, 36025, 323, 72741, 432, 304, 624], "logp_list": [-0.0, -3.2615, -0.3603, -0.0269, -0.5702, -0.0016, -0.0052, -0.2693, -0.0074, -4.0238, -0.0006, -0.51, -1.7296, -0.018, -0.9256, -0.2451, -0.1909, -0.0257, -0.7848, -0.3613, -0.2423, -0.0014, -0.2245, -0.0066, -0.662, -0.5907, -0.457, -0.0, -0.3275, -0.0198, -0.5746, -0.2296, -0.8303, -0.3143, -0.0084, -0.0495, -2.4866, -0.1028, -0.0119, -0.0, -1.6864, -0.0086, -0.2219, -0.0209, -1.1018, -0.0