{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "To make ribs, start by selecting the main ingredients, such as ribs and seasonings. Depending on the type of ribs, determine the cooking method, which could include grilling, baking, or braising. Prepare the ribs by trimming excess fat and thoroughly washing them. Season the ribs with desired spices and herbs to enhance the flavor. Cook the ribs using the chosen method, keeping an eye on the cooking process and making adjustments to heat and timing as needed. Finally, allow the ribs to rest for a few minutes before serving to ensure they are tender and flavorful.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To make ribs, start by selecting the main ingredients, such as ribs and seasonings. Depending on the type of ribs, determine the cooking method, which could include grilling, baking, or braising. Prepare the ribs by trimming excess fat and thoroughly washing them. Season the ribs with desired spices and herbs to enhance the flavor. Cook the ribs using the chosen method, keeping an eye on the cooking process and making adjustments to heat and timing as needed. Finally, allow the ribs to rest for a few minutes before serving to ensure they are tender and flavorful.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the main ingredients required for making ribs.\n2. Determine the cooking method based on the type of ribs (e.g., beef, pork, chicken).\n3. Prepare the ribs by trimming excess fat and washing them thoroughly.\n4. Season the ribs with desired spices and herbs for flavor.\n5. Cook the ribs using the chosen method (e.g., grilling, baking, braising).\n6. Monitor the cooking process, adjusting heat and timing as needed.\n7. Allow the ribs to rest for a few minutes before serving to enhance tenderness and flavor.\nAnswer: To make ribs, start by identifying the main ingredients required, such as ribs and seasonings. Then, determine the cooking method based on the type of ribs, such as grilling, baking, or braising. Prepare the ribs by trimming excess fat and washing them thoroughly. Season the ribs with desired spices and herbs for flavor. Cook the ribs using the chosen method, monitoring the cooking process and adjusting heat and timing as needed. Finally, allow the ribs to rest for a few minutes before serving to enhance tenderness and flavor.\nTo make ribs, start by selecting the main ingredients, such as ribs and seasonings. Depending on the type of ribs, determine the cooking method, which could include grilling, baking, or braising. Prepare the ribs by trimming excess fat and thoroughly washing them. Season the ribs with desired spices and herbs to enhance the flavor. Cook the ribs using the chosen method, keeping an eye on the cooking process and making adjustments to heat and timing as needed. Finally, allow the ribs to rest for a few minutes before serving to ensure they are tender and flavorful.\n\nAnswer: To make ribs, start by selecting the main ingredients, such as ribs and seasonings. Depending on the type of ribs, determine the cooking method, which could include grilling, baking, or braising. Prepare the ribs by trimming excess fat and thoroughly washing them. Season the ribs with desired spices and herbs to enhance the flavor. Cook the ribs using the chosen method, keeping an eye on the cooking process and making adjustments to heat and timing as needed. Finally, allow the ribs to rest for a few minutes before serving to ensure they are tender and flavorful.", "time_sec": 30.512, "generation_time_seconds": 30.4769, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0291, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 12, 4457, 1526, 279, 46769, 3897, 311, 3535, 279, 2266, 323, 9567, 9760, 1995, 911, 3259, 55149, 624, 12, 64547, 279, 1376, 5424, 9733, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 1741, 438, 13966, 11, 17233, 5413, 11, 323, 3151, 7354, 624, 12, 10762, 551, 279, 1995, 1119, 264, 55787, 8500, 429, 16555, 279, 1882, 315, 3259, 55149, 624, 12, 29279, 429, 678, 7354, 525, 7248, 553, 279, 3565, 2661, 304, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 34006, 7842, 9250, 1995, 476, 3259, 31846, 537, 5961, 7248, 553, 279, 46769, 624, 12, 1416, 279, 46769, 653, 537, 6644, 3322, 1995, 311, 4226, 279, 3405, 11, 31094, 448, 330, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 1189, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -2.6942, -2.0984, -1.0827, -0.0006, -3.3595, -2.8729, -0.1387, -2.1383, -0.0127, -0.0558, -0.0162, -1.9762, -0.7005, -0.0102, -0.561, -0.0526, -0.0, -0.0504, -0.0009, -0.0199, -1.461, -0.2753, -2.8828, -2.716, -0.0107, -0.0003, -0.0118, -1.7003, -0.0002, 0.0, -0.1064, -0.0002, -0.1966, -0.0204, -0.0, -0.5994, -0.6651, -1.2389, -0.5992, -0.0, -0.645, 0.0, -0.0096, -0.0128, -1.8569, -0.0013, -1.2724, -0.0362, -0.3359, -2.3023, -0.2136, -0.0026, -0.0022, -0.003, -0.0, -0.0171, -0.0002, -0.3283, -0.0616, -1.855, -1.5547, -0.1034, -0.4181, -0.0, -0.1251, -1.5594, -0.2403, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.4356, -0.0008, -2.5401, -0.1043, -0.2435, -0.001