{"id": "510", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their location within the sirloin muscle. Sirloin steaks are cut from the back of the animal and continue off the short loin from which other cuts such as T-bone and porterhouse steaks are made. On the other hand, porterhouse steaks are specifically carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin and therefore have more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-bone steaks. However, the passages suggest that both sirloin and porterhouse steaks may be referred to as the same thing or as a large version of the T-bone due to their similarity in appearance and taste.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the primary characteristics of sirloin steak.\n2. Identify the primary characteristics of porterhouse steak.\n3. Compare the two steaks to determine the differences.\n4. Provide specific examples, numbers, or comparisons where applicable.\n5. Ensure all details supporting the answer are included.\n6. If the passages do not contain sufficient information, answer: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"\n7. Output the final answer after completing the analysis. Answer:[Your answer here]\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 39.797, "generation_time_seconds": 39.7561, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0348, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151