{"id": "645", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "pred": "Monitor the potato's growth and gradually increase the soil depth around it as it starts to grow new sprouts, usually 2-3 weeks after planting.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Monitor the potato's growth and gradually increase the soil depth around it as it starts to grow new sprouts, usually 2-3 weeks after planting.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Ensure the potato has sprouted visibly and is healthy.\n2. Choose a suitable planting location with good drainage.\n3. Prepare the soil by turning it over and adding compost or fertilizer for nutrients.\n4. Dig a hole about 4-6 inches deep, depending on the size of the potato.\n5. Place the sprouted potato in the hole with the sprout facing upwards.\n6. Cover the potato with soil, leaving only the sprout exposed.\n7. Water the potato gently and keep the soil moist but not waterlogged.\n8. Monitor the potato's growth and gradually increase the soil depth around it as it\nstarts to grow new sprouts, usually 2-3 weeks after planting.\nAnswer: Monitor the potato's growth and gradually increase the soil depth around it as it starts to grow new sprouts, usually 2-3 weeks after planting.\n\nAnswer: Monitor the potato's growth and gradually increase the soil depth around it as it starts to grow new sprouts, usually 2-3 weeks after planting.", "time_sec": 14.907, "generation_time_seconds": 14.8703, "selection_time_seconds": 0.029, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 25, 29901, 892, 38734, 702, 8151, 18533, 13, 9192, 369, 9434, 67443, 476, 6176, 43627, 23206, 504, 279, 38734, 594, 7329, 13, 1096, 374, 16587, 311, 5978, 498, 525, 47014, 279, 4396, 38734, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.9105, -0.0002, -0.3594, -0.0097, -0.2791, -0.0065, -0.0036, -0.1272, -2.327, -0.0835, -0.1659, -0.1191, -0.0051, -0.001, -3.361, -0.7626, -0.0, -0.5409, -3.0262, -0.0043, -2.0445, -0.0889, -0.0045, -0.0, -0.0019, -0.4861, -0.4816, -0.2402, -2.2711, -0.4855, -0.646, -2.415, -1.1638, -0.3299, -0.2392, -0.2238, -0.0448, -0.4328, -0.0953, -0.0336, -0.3904, -Infinity, -Infinity, -15.4066, -19.3751, -20.9707, -12.7084, -11.9847, -7.0018, -11.0722, -10.8647, -8.0705, -7.311, -6.5635, -7.083, -7.4002, -5.2329, -3.345, -3.149, -3.2548, -4.846, -6.3097, -7.5828, -7.7791, -8.0919, -8.4384, -7.049, -5.3726, -4.6089, -4.82, -5.7041, -4.6494, -3.9696, -3.0128, -3.076, -4.9063, -5.8393, -6.1578, -4.4916, -2.8526, -2.5552, -3.3532, -4.4769, 