{"id": "63", "question": "set default browser to windows", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "The final answer is \"Confirm the selection: Ensure the browser is set as the default and confirm the selection to apply the changes.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The final answer is \"Confirm the selection: Ensure the browser is set as the default and confirm the selection to apply the changes.\"", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the current default browser: Check the system settings or the start menu to find out which browser is currently set as the default.\n2. Open the Settings: Access the operating system settings where you can manage applications and settings.\n3. Find the Default App settings: Look for an option related to default applications or settings.\n4. Select the browser: Choose the desired browser from the list of installed applications.\n5. Confirm the selection: Ensure the browser is set as the default and confirm the selection to apply the changes.\nThe next logical step would be to select the browser you want to set as the default from the list of installed applications. This step is crucial as it directly impacts the final outcome of setting the default browser. By choosing the correct browser, you ensure that it will be the preferred choice when opening links and documents in the operating system.\nConfirm the selection: Ensure the browser is set as the default and confirm the selection to apply the changes.\n\nAnswer: The final answer is \"Confirm the selection: Ensure the browser is set as the default and confirm the selection to apply the changes.\"", "time_sec": 14.34, "generation_time_seconds": 14.2821, "selection_time_seconds": 0.05, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.5045, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0043, -0.0006, -24.5833, -19.1271, -8.229, -12.0325, -7.0856, -8.8159, -9.002, -7.138, -6.9297, -6.3702, -6.8205, -6.6374, -4.6055, -1.8946, -2.