{"id": "77", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and continue cooking on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "pred": "To cook brats, first determine the type of bratwurst (e.g., beef, pork, chicken). Preheat the cooking surface to the correct temperature for the chosen cooking method. Prepare the bratwursts by cleaning them and removing any excess casing if necessary. Choose a cooking method, such as cooking on the stove or grill. If cooking on the stove, place the bratwursts in a pot and add water or beer to cover about a quarter of the bratwursts. Bring to a boil and then reduce the heat to a simmer. Cook for about 20-30 minutes, or until the bratwursts are cooked through. Flip the bratwursts occasionally to ensure even cooking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To cook brats, first determine the type of bratwurst (e.g., beef, pork, chicken). Preheat the cooking surface to the correct temperature for the chosen cooking method. Prepare the bratwursts by cleaning them and removing any excess casing if necessary. Choose a cooking method, such as cooking on the stove or grill. If cooking on the stove, place the bratwursts in a pot and add water or beer to cover about a quarter of the bratwursts. Bring to a boil and then reduce the heat to a simmer. Cook for about 20-30 minutes, or until the bratwursts are cooked through. Flip the bratwursts occasionally to ensure even cooking.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Determine the type of bratwurst: The type of bratwurst (e.g., beef, pork, chicken) affects the cooking method and timing.\n2. Preheat the cooking surface: Ensure the stove or grill is preheated to the correct temperature for the cooking method.\n3. Prepare the bratwursts: Clean the bratwursts and remove any excess casing if necessary.\n4. Choose a cooking method: Decide whether to cook the bratwursts on the stove, grill, or in the oven.\n5. Cook on the stove: Place the bratwurst\n5. Cook on the stove: Place the bratwursts in a pot on the stove and add water or beer to cover about a quarter of the bratwursts. Bring to a boil and then reduce the heat to a simmer. Cook for about 20-30 minutes, or until the bratwursts are cooked through. Flip the bratwursts occasionally to ensure even cooking.\nCooking on the stove: Place the bratwursts in a pot on the stove and add water or beer to cover about a quarter of the bratwursts. Bring to a boil and then reduce the heat to a simmer. Cook for about 20-30 minutes, or until the bratwursts are cooked through. Flip the bratwursts occasionally to ensure even cooking.\n\nAnswer: To cook brats, first determine the type of bratwurst (e.g., beef, pork, chicken). Preheat the cooking surface to the correct temperature for the chosen cooking method. Prepare the bratwursts by cleaning them and removing any excess casing if necessary. Choose a cooking method, such as cooking on the stove or grill. If cooking on the stove, place the bratwursts in a pot and add water or beer to cover about a quarter of the bratwursts. Bring to a boil and then reduce the heat to a simmer. Cook for about 20-30 minutes, or until the bratwursts are cooked through. Flip the bratwursts occasionally to ensure even cooking.", "time_sec": 24.246, "generation_time_seconds": 24.1967, "selection_time_seconds": 0.04, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 29901, 279, 943, 315, 1411, 2