{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "The final answer is not provided in the given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The final answer is not provided in the given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the purpose of the shed and its intended use.\n2. Determine the materials needed for the shed, such as wood, nails, and a metal roof.\n3. Sketch a plan for the shed, including the dimensions and placement of the walls and roof.\n4. Gather the necessary tools, such as a saw, hammer, and drill.\n5. Begin construction by preparing the foundation and framing the walls.\n6. Assemble the walls and attach the roof to the frame.\n7. Install the doors and windows, if necessary.\n8. Add finishing touches, such as painting or staining the wood.\n9. Secure the\nroof by nailing it in place.\n10. Install any remaining accessories, such as shelves, hooks, or a latch for the door.\n11. Inspect the shed for any loose components or areas that need additional reinforcement.\n12. Apply a final coat of paint or stain to protect the wood from the elements.\n13. Allow the paint or stain to dry completely before using the shed.\n14. Optionally, add a floor to the shed if it will be used for storage or other purposes.\n15. Place the shed on its foundation and ensure it is level and secure.\n16. Connect the shed to the house or property, if necessary, using support beams or other methods.\n17. Install any remaining fixtures or accessories, such as a light fixture or a power outlet.\n18. Clean up the work area and dispose of any waste materials.\n19. Inspect the shed again for any final adjustments or repairs that may be needed.\n20. Enjoy your new, functional lean-to shed.\n\nAnswer: The final answer is not provided in the given passages.", "time_sec": 19.048, "generation_time_seconds": 18.9743, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0492, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.4876, -0.012, -0.0003, -0.0001, -0.3759, -9.1131, -14.8348, -10.8335, -8.3336, -5.2494, -4.7813, -4.106, -6.3325, -3.502, -0.9718, -0.5749, -0.7299, -0.90