{"id": "137", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "pred": "Gather the necessary ingredients and tools.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Gather the necessary ingredients and tools.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the method of roasting individual garlic cloves.\n2. Gather the necessary ingredients and tools.\n3. Prepare the garlic cloves.\n4. Roast the garlic cloves.\n5. Serve the roasted garlic cloves.\nThe next logical reasoning step is:\nGather the necessary ingredients and tools.\n\nAnswer: Gather the necessary ingredients and tools.", "time_sec": 28.181, "generation_time_seconds": 28.1227, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0414, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516