{"id": "303", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Understand the components of the hot water heater system.\n2. Identify the specific issue related to the circulation of hot water in the system.\n3. Determine if the issue is related to the flow, temperature, or pressure of the water.\n4. Check the current setup and configuration of the hot water heater system.\n5. Research and identify common troubleshooting methods and solutions for the identified issue.\n6. Apply the identified solutions, such as adjusting settings, replacing components, or performing maintenance tasks.\n7. Monitor the results and make adjustments as necessary to ensure proper circulation of hot water. Answer: [Your answer here]\nThe reasoning steps are:\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.997, "generation_time_seconds": 18.9454, "selection_time_seconds": 0.043, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516