{"id": "361", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "The main difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is the timing of the attack. Ad hominem fallacy attacks the person making the argument instead of attacking the argument directly, but poisoning the well fallacy is a preemptive attack on a person's character or integrity before they have even made their argument. In other words, ad hominem fallacy is a reaction to an argument, while poisoning the well fallacy is a preemptive strike to discredit an opponent before they have a chance to present their argument.", "pred": "Define ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Define ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nDefine ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy.\nPlease generate the NEXT logical reasoning step. Do NOT provide the final answer yet. Focus strictly on analyzing the physical details step by step.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nDefine ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy.", "time_sec": 36.466, "generation_time_seconds": 36.3934, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0525, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [0.0, -0.7606, -0.0085, -0.0007, -0.0002, -1.9437, -Infinity, -16.156, -11.251, -7.0844, -6.1447, -5.8126, -3.3697, -4.8956, -3.4618], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 153, "output_tokens": 15}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], 