{"id": "383", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an excel sheet alphabetical, one can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n5. The data should now be sorted in alphabetical order.", "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the column(s) that need to be sorted alphabetically.\n2. Click on the column header to select the column(s) for sorting.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon.\n4. Click on \"Sort\" in the Data tab.\n5. In the Sort dialog box, select \"A to Z\" or \"Z to A\" depending on the desired sorting order.\n6. Click \"OK\" to sort the selected column(s) alphabetically.\n7. Verify the results by checking the first few rows of the sorted column(s).", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the column(s) that need to be sorted alphabetically.\n2. Click on the column header to select the column(s) for sorting.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon.\n4. Click on \"Sort\" in the Data tab.\n5. In the Sort dialog box, select \"A to Z\" or \"Z to A\" depending on the desired sorting order.\n6. Click \"OK\" to sort the selected column(s) alphabetically.\n7. Verify the results by checking the first few rows of the sorted column(s).\n7. Verify the results by checking the first few rows of the sorted column(s).\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the column(s) that need to be sorted alphabetically.\n2. Click on the column header to select the column(s) for sorting.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon.\n4. Click on \"Sort\" in the Data tab.\n5. In the Sort dialog box, select \"A to Z\" or \"Z to A\" depending on the desired sorting order.\n6. Click \"OK\" to sort the selected column(s) alphabetically.\n7. Verify the results by checking the first few rows of the sorted column(s).", "time_sec": 18.303, "generation_time_seconds": 18.2576, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0307, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 3250, 1141, 8, 429, 1184, 311, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 3250, 4247, 311, 3293, 279, 3250, 1141, 8, 369, 28273, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 1043, 1, 5651, 304, 279, 21029, 44567, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 330, 10231, 1, 304, 279, 2885, 5651, 624, 20, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 7254, 3745, 11, 3293, 330, 32, 311, 1863, 1, 476, 330, 57, 311, 362, 1, 11649, 389, 279, 12685, 28273, 1973, 624, 21, 13, 9189, 330, 3925, 1, 311, 3378, 279, 4091, 3250, 1141, 8, 27790, 2673, 624, 22, 13, 25429, 279, 3059, 553, 13295, 279, 1156, 2421, 6978, 315, 279, 10615, 3250, 1141, 568, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -0.9884, -0.0001, -0.1625, -0.0006, -1.1032, -2.3153, -0.0, -1.5158, -0.3534, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.0618, -0.0084, 0.0, -0.1159, -0.0033, 0.0, -1.0906, -0.0039, -0.0048, -0.4539, -0.0067, -0.4041, -0.0661, -0.2109, -0.9498, -0.0551, -0.1433, -0.6609, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.0001, -0.0, -1.7315, -0.0791, -0.0003, -0.0829, -0.1179, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.013, -0.0, -0.0357, -0.0066, -0.0132, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1767, -0.0017, -1.5019, -0.0, -0.394, -0.1696, 0.0, -0.9267, -0.099, -0.0391, -0.0001, 0.0, -1.0294, 0.0, -0.8062, -0.0111, -0.0002, -0.0004, -0.319, -0.8033, -0.9668, -0.0362, 0.0, -0.0, -0.6081, -0.0009, -0.0322, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.1693, -0.0, -0.0196, -0.0071, -2.4528, -0.001, -0.0132, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0073, -0.01