{"id": "433", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\n\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth to shine silver jewelry that is merely dull or starting to discolor. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. Use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. Pat the jewelry dry with a soft cloth.\n3. Soak tarnished silver jewelry in a saltwater solution of two cups of hot water. This method is gentle and can remove tarnish without abrading the silver. Make sure the gemstones will not be affected by the solution before submerging them.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to clean other types of jewelry, such as gold or platinum, or what to do if the tarnish is heavy or if the jewelry has intricate designs that may be damaged during cleaning.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps: Identify the type of metal (silver, gold, etc.), assess the extent of tarnish, determine if the jewelry is delicate, gather appropriate cleaning materials, prepare the cleaning solution or powder, test the method on a small area, apply the cleaning solution or powder, gently rub with a cloth or brush, let it sit for the recommended time, rinse with warm water, dry thoroughly, store in a dry, acid-free environment, and repeat if needed.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps: Identify the type of metal (silver, gold, etc.), assess the extent of tarnish, determine if the jewelry is delicate, gather appropriate cleaning materials, prepare the cleaning solution or powder, test the method on a small area, apply the cleaning solution or powder, gently rub with a cloth or brush, let it sit for the recommended time, rinse with warm water, dry thoroughly, store in a dry, acid-free environment, and repeat if needed.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the type of tarnished jewelry you have (e.g., silver, gold, or other metals).\n2. Assess the extent of tarnish on the jewelry. Is it minor or extensive?\n3. Determine if the jewelry is delicate or has complex designs. This will affect the cleaning method.\n4. Gather appropriate cleaning materials for the type of metal and the extent of the tarnish.\n5. Prepare the cleaning solution or powder based on the type of metal and the cleaning method chosen.\n6. Test the cleaning method on a small, inconspicuous area of the jewelry to ensure it does not damage the metal.\n7. Begin cleaning the jewelry by applying the cleaning solution or powder to the tarnished areas.\n8. Use a soft cloth or brush to gently rub the cleaning solution or powder into the tarnished areas.\n9. Let the jewelry sit for the recommended time to allow the cleaning solution to work on the tarnish.\n10. Rinse the jewelry with warm water to remove any cleaning solution or powder residue.\n11. Dry the jewelry thoroughly with a soft cloth to prevent water spots.\n12. Store the jewelry in a dry, acid-free environment to prevent further tarnishing.\n13. Repeat the cleaning process if the tarn\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps: Identify the type of metal (silver, gold, etc.), assess the extent of tarnish, determine if the jewelry is delicate, gather appropriate cleaning materials, prepare the cleaning solution or powder, test the method on a small area, apply the cleaning solution or powder, gently rub with a cloth or brush, let it sit for the recommended time, rinse with warm water, dry thoroughly, store in a dry, acid-free environment, and repeat if needed.\n\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps: Identify the type of metal (silver, gold, etc.), assess the extent of tarnish, determine if the jewelry is delicate, gather appropriate cleaning materials, prepare the cleaning solution or powder, test the method on a small area, apply the cleaning solution or powder, gently rub with a cloth or brush, let it sit for the recommended time, rinse with warm water, dry thoroughly, store in a dry, acid-free environment, and repeat if needed.", "time_sec": 22.529, "generation_time_seconds": 22.4829, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0383, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 86480, 3304, 30717, 498, 614, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 14961, 11, 6623, 11, 476, 1008, 36082, 4292, 17, 13, 81835, 279, 12818, 315, 86480, 812, 389, 279, 30717, 13, 2160, 432, 8922, 476, 16376, 5267, 18, 13, 29901, 421, 279, 30717, 374, 35201, 476, 702, 6351, 14431, 13, 1096, 686, 7802, 279, 15826, 1714, 624, 19, 13, 48995, 8311, 15826, 7236, 369, 279, 943, 315, 9317, 323, 279, 12818, 315, 279, 86480, 812, 624, 20, 13, 31166, 279, 15826, 6291, 476, 16723, 3118, 389, 279, 943, 315, 9317, 323, 279, 15826, 1714, 11882, 624, 21, 13, 3393, 279, 15826, 1714, 389, 264, 2613, 11, 26995, 2154, 292, 9193, 3082, 315, 279, 30717, 311, 5978, 432, 1558, 537, 5557, 279, 9317, 624], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.3441, -0.0002, -0.1044, -0.0096, -0.0608, -0.0013, -1.6435, -0.8028, -0.003, -3.6351, -0.1751, -2.2998, -0.0853, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0795, -0.0003, -0.0152, -0.0435, -0.2199, -0.3012, -0.0843, -0.1126, -0.0015, 0.0, -3.896, -0.0006, -0.9797, -0.0013, -1.5019, -0.3023, -1.0404, -0.0078, -0.0001, -1.1841, -0.8863, -0.0063, -4.5304, -0.524, -0.8101, -0.1424, -0.0001, 0.0, -1.1434, -0.5384, -0.0657, -0.1427, -0.2795, -0.4895, -0.1378, -0.725, -5.4745, -0.1962, -2.984, -0.2339, -0.1062, -0.0623, -0.031, -0.028, -0.0145, -0.9409, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.6086, -0.2454, -0.0063, -0.5507, -4.2171, -0.1184, -0.1767, -0.0645, -0.1789, -0.0989, -0.2074, -1.4115, -0.0, -3.5704, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.4