{"id": "516", "question": "history of the word gemini", "gt": "Sure! Here's a brief history of the word Gemini based on the given passages:\n\nThe word \"Gemini\" comes from Latin, meaning \"twins.\" The constellation Gemini was first mentioned in Aristotle's Meteorologica over 300 years BC. In Greek mythology, the twins represented in Gemini are Castor and Pollux, who share the same mother, Leda, but have different fathers. The constellation Gemini is not in the same position as the constellation of Gemini and is a mutable sign that announces change and rules the time of year when Taurus spring has ended.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you need further clarification or if there's anything else I can help you with.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the key information about the word \"Gemini\" from the given passage.\n2. Determine if the passage provides enough details to trace the history of the word \"Gemini.\"\n3. If the passage does not provide sufficient information, conclude that the question cannot be answered with the given text.\nGiven the steps outlined, the next logical reasoning step is:\nIdentify any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons mentioned in the passage that relate to the use or development of the word \"Gemini.\"\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 9.616, "generation_time_seconds": 9.5844, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0268, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 1376, 1995, 911, 279, 3409, 330, 95040, 6591, 1, 504, 279, 2661, 21085, 624, 17, 13, 29901, 421, 279, 21085, 5707, 3322, 3565, 311, 11655, 279, 3840, 315, 279, 3409, 330, 95040, 6591, 10040, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 21085, 1558, 537, 