{"id": "573", "question": "how to quickly get rid of mice", "gt": "To quickly get rid of mice, you need to take immediate action. You can start by identifying all possible entry points that mice use to get into your house. Once identified, consider putting steel wool inside these holes or vents before sealing them off. This will prevent the mice from using these paths to re-enter your home. By doing so, you eliminate their access to food or shelter in your house, which can help in getting rid of them quickly.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the problem (mice presence)\nStep 2: Determine the effectiveness of current methods (if any)\nStep 3: Research alternative methods for quick mouse removal\nStep 4: Evaluate the feasibility and safety of each method\nStep 5: Select the most effective and safe method\nStep 6: Implement the chosen method\nStep 7: Monitor the results and adjust as necessary\nStep 8: Document the process and outcomes for future reference\nStep 9: Continue monitoring and adjusting the method as needed\nStep 10: Consider using traps or barriers to prevent future infestations\nStep 11: Educate others about mouse prevention measures\nStep 12: Evaluate the overall effectiveness of the chosen method\nStep 13: Document the entire process and outcomes for future reference\nStep 14: Share the findings with relevant authorities or communities\nStep 15: Consider long-term solutions for ongoing pest management\nStep 16: Implement long-term solutions for ongoing pest management, if deemed necessary\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 16.946, "generation_time_seconds": 16.9022, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0369, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0,