{"id": "646", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, follow these steps:\n\n1. Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each using a sharp knife.\n2. Set the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and allow them to dry out for a cool, dark location overnight.\n3. Once the cut ends are dry, thoroughly wash the potatoes.\n4. Plant the potatoes in the ground, either whole or cut into cubes with a sprout on each cube.\n5. Space the potatoes about 6 to 8 inches apart and cover them with a layer of compost.\n6. Replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n7. Water the potatoes regularly when the soil is dry to the touch.\n8. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the stage of the potato's growth.\nStep 2: Prepare the planting area by selecting a suitable spot with good drainage and sunlight.\nStep 3: Prepare the potato for planting by cutting it into sections, ensuring each piece has at least one sprout.\nStep 4: Plant the sprouted potato pieces in the prepared soil, spacing them appropriately.\nStep 5: Cover the potato pieces with a layer of soil, leaving the sprouts exposed.\nStep 6: Water the newly planted potatoes gently to ensure they are moist without causing soil erosion.\nStep 7: Continue to monitor the growth of the\nsprouts. As the sprouts grow, provide them with adequate nutrients by fertilizing the soil, and ensure they receive enough water to maintain healthy growth. If the sprouts develop leaves, you can begin to harvest the potatoes as they mature, typically when the stems turn yellow and the potatoes are firm.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 28.829, "generation_time_seconds": 28.7848, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0329, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 12, 64547, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 198, 12, 22201, 264, 14452, 47014, 3728, 198, 12, 31166, 279, 17171, 198, 12, 17838, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 198, 12, 17757, 279, 38734, 448, 17171, 198, 12, 9959, 279, 38734, 198, 12, 86377, 279, 38734, 6008, 198, 12, 39565, 39020, 323, 36393, 271, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -3.723, -0.2227, -0.0042, -0.6999, -0.0111, -0.0235, -1.3287, -0.0002, -0.0973, -0.0974, -0.0024, -0.3853, -0.2839, -0.1194, -0.0, -0.0086, -0.0005, -0.2093, -0.2689, -0.0, -0.7913, -0.0001, -0.3023, -0.0013, -0.0, -0.0453, -0.0, -0.1069, -0.3758, -0.0683, -0.0152, -0.0001, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0033, -0.1764, -0.228, -0.178, -0.0006, -1.1763, -0.1202, -0.0946, -0.164, -0.5862, -0.0647, -3.6702, -1.5418, -0.059, -0.1831, -1.8521, -Infinity, -17.7166, -17.7731, -14.3758, -23.8542, -12.8314, -3.5457, -8.9594, -9.5481, -8.8465, -5.3907, -7.3865, -9.8857, -11.5229, -10.4518, -6.4723, -4.4316, -4.3238, -4.6401, -5.4454, -6.5635, -7.7262, -7.311, -5.4199, -4.9891, -3.9228, -3.5716, -6.8519, -7.6228, -6.3897, -5.2758, -4.8444, -4.6264, -7.3002, -9.7987, -9.3877, -7.097, -5.8558, -4