{"id": "666", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "When you breathe in, your diaphragm contracts and pulls downwards, expanding the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also contract to expand the ribcage. Pressure inside the chest is reduced, causing air to be sucked into the lungs. On the other hand, when you breathe out, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, reducing the space in the chest cavity. Air rich in carbon dioxide is then forced out of the lungs and windpipe. Breathing out does not require any effort from your body unless you have a lung disease or are doing physical activity.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the specific details about breathing in and out that are provided in the passage.\n2. Determine if there is enough information to describe what happens during these processes.\n3. If there is sufficient information, provide a detailed description of the actions involved in breathing in and out, including any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons mentioned.\n4. If there is not enough information to describe breathing in and out, state that it is unable to answer based on the given passages.\nThe passage does not provide specific details about what happens when you breathe in and out. It only asks to describe what happens during these processes. Since there is no additional information provided in the passage, I cannot answer the question based on the given information.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 13.106, "generation_time_seconds": 13.0589, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0406, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam":