{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "The next logical reasoning step is to check for any obstructions, such as debris or dust, that may be preventing the door from locking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The next logical reasoning step is to check for any obstructions, such as debris or dust, that may be preventing the door from locking.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Determine the cause of the problem: Is the door jammed, or is the lock mechanism failing?\n2. Inspect the door and frame for any physical damage or misalignment.\n3. Check the lock mechanism for any signs of wear or damage, such as broken pins or worn-out tumblers.\n4. Ensure that the door is installed correctly and that the frame is square and level.\n5. Verify that the door hardware (hinges, screws, and latches) is securely fastened and functioning properly.\n6. Check for any obstructions, such as debris or dust, that may be preventing the door from locking\n7. Adjust or replace any damaged or worn-out lock components, such as pins, tumblers, or springs, as necessary.\n8. Clean the lock mechanism and surrounding area to remove any debris or dust that may be causing the door to jam.\n9. Secure the door hardware, such as hinges and latches, by tightening screws or bolts to ensure they are properly aligned and functioning.\n10. Test the door to ensure that it is operating smoothly and locking properly. If the problem persists, repeat the inspection and adjustment process as needed.\nAnswer: The next logical reasoning step is to check for any obstructions, such as debris or dust, that may be preventing the door from locking.\n\nAnswer: The next logical reasoning step is to check for any obstructions, such as debris or dust, that may be preventing the door from locking.", "time_sec": 27.609, "generation_time_seconds": 27.2022, "selection_time_seconds": 0.3578, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 29901, 279, 5240, 315, 279, 3491, 25, 2160, 279, 6006, 20072, 2061, 11, 476, 374, 279, 5296, 16953, 21394, 5267, 17, 13, 9726, 987, 279, 6006, 323, 4034, 369, 894, 6961, 5557, 476, 5786, 44598, 624, 18, 13, 4248, 279, 5296, 16953, 369, 894, 11929, 315, 9850, 476, 5557, 11, 1741, 438, 10865, 26944, 476, 23704, 9794, 15394, 70378, 624, 19, 13, 29279, 429, 279, 6006, 374, 10275, 12440, 323, 429, 279, 4034, 374, 9334, 323, 2188, 624, 20, 13, 25429, 429, 279, 6006, 11773, 320, 71, 40399, 11, 44922, 11, 323, 326, 9118, 8, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 323, 30201, 10277, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 894, 1508, 19657, 11, 1741, 438, 33998, 476, 15797, 11, 429, 1231, 387, 26160, 279, 6006, 504, 37855], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.2572, -0.0003, -3.5626, -0.2613, -1.4832, -0.0055, -0.0001, -0.7184, -0.1931, -2.1976, -0.0851, -0.3345, -2.4747, -0.0102, -0.0368, -2.3401, -0.0214, -1.0962, -0.2113, -0.9245, -5.3114, -0.4734, -0.0047, -0.0, -1.3797, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0177, -1.0434, -1.0257, -0.7041, -0.0294, -1.0412, -0.2699, -0.0729, -0.0291, -0.0, -0.4361, -0.0008, -0.0, -0.0211, -0.1014, -0.1627, -0.3349, -0.103, -0.1872, -0.3525, 0.