{"id": "127", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Sure! Here's my attempt to answer your question based on the provided passages:\n\nHow do you prepare the site for building a lean-to shed?\n\nAccording to passage 1, step 1, you should prepare the site by laying down a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. This will provide a stable base for the shed's foundation. Additionally, passage 2 mentions cutting two pressure-treated 4x4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids, which will serve as the foundation for the shed. Finally, passage 3 provides instructions for building the shed's floor, including cutting rim joists to a length of 6 feet. Based on these passages, it appears that preparing the site involves laying down a layer of gravel and setting the skids in place before constructing the floor.", "pred": "Install the floor and insulation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Install the floor and insulation.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the purpose and size of the lean-to shed\n2. Gather materials and tools needed for construction\n3. Measure and prepare the site\n4. Build the foundation\n5. Construct the frame\n6. Add siding and roofing\n7. Install doors and windows\n8. Add any finishing touches\nThe next logical reasoning step is:\n9. Install the floor and insulation\n\nAnswer: Install the floor and insulation.", "time_sec": 18.765, "generation_time_seconds": 18.7187, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0359, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516