{"id": "296", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which can have a large amount of kinetic energy due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy. Other activities like a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit also involve potential and kinetic energy.", "pred": "Potential energy examples include an object elevated above the ground, which has gravitational potential energy, and a stretched spring, which has elastic potential energy. Kinetic energy examples include the energy of a moving ball, a moving car, a falling apple, and a cyclist.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Potential energy examples include an object elevated above the ground, which has gravitational potential energy, and a stretched spring, which has elastic potential energy. Kinetic energy examples include the energy of a moving ball, a moving car, a falling apple, and a cyclist.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the types of energy mentioned: The question asks about potential and kinetic energy. \n2. Recall the definitions: \n   - Potential energy is stored energy that depends on the position or configuration of an object. \n   - Kinetic energy is the energy of motion.\n3. Consider examples of potential energy:\n   - Gravitational potential energy: An object elevated above the ground has potential energy due to its position relative to the Earth's surface.\n   - Elastic potential energy: A stretched or compressed spring has potential energy due to the deformation.\n4. Consider examples of kinetic energy:\n   - The energy of a moving ball\n5. Expand on kinetic energy examples:\n   - A moving car has kinetic energy due to its motion.\n   - A falling apple in the air has kinetic energy due to its motion towards the ground.\n   - A cyclist has kinetic energy due to the motion of the bicycle and the rider.\nAnswer: Potential energy examples include an object elevated above the ground, which has gravitational potential energy, and a stretched spring, which has elastic potential energy. Kinetic energy examples include the energy of a moving ball, a moving car, a falling apple, and a cyclist.\n\nAnswer: Potential energy examples include an object elevated above the ground, which has gravitational potential energy, and a stretched spring, which has elastic potential energy. Kinetic energy examples include the energy of a moving ball, a moving car, a falling apple, and a cyclist.", "time_sec": 17.697, "generation_time_seconds": 17.6499, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0375, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 24391, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 15164