{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "The growth of the watermelon to a certain size and the pressure of the inside of the watermelon exceeding the strength of the rind.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The growth of the watermelon to a certain size and the pressure of the inside of the watermelon exceeding the strength of the rind.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nWatermelon explosions are caused by the growth of the watermelon to a certain size and the pressure of the inside of the watermelon exceeding the strength of the rind.\n\nAnswer: The growth of the watermelon to a certain size and the pressure of the inside of the watermelon exceeding the strength of the rind.", "time_sec": 25.255, "generation_time_seconds": 25.2095, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0382, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 5501, 3410, 279, 1790, 19819, 32711, 3019, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 1995, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -3.5222, -0.3652, -0.0055, -0.0734, -0.0021, -0.0083, -0.0001, -1.1669, -0.0, -0.0003, -0.2155, -0.7632, -0.0244, -0.0258], "cumulative_logprob": -6.1729, "norm_logp": -0.4115, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 15}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 