{"id": "340", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the main ingredients for making ribs.\n2. Determine the cooking method for ribs, such as baking, grilling, or smoking.\n3. Explain any necessary preparation steps, such as trimming fat or marinating the ribs.\n4. Provide specific instructions or tips for cooking the ribs, such as cooking time or temperature.\n5. Include any additional details or variations for the recipe.\nThe next logical reasoning step is:\nTo identify the main ingredients for making ribs, we need to look for a list of ingredients that are commonly used in rib recipes.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 17.187, "generation_time_seconds": 17.1488, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0325, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 785, 32711, 7354, 525, 510, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 13966, 4362, 369, 3259, 55149, 624, 17, 13, 31166, 279, 55149, 553, 15826, 323, 86219, 1105, 624, 18, 13, 12514, 279, 55149, 1667, 264, 11882, 17233, 1714, 11, 1741, 438, 1081, 9400, 11, 27815, 11, 476, 6301, 22471, 10746, 624, 19, 13, 52932, 279, 55149, 448, 894, 14890, 5725, 848, 12558, 476, 89970, 13, 21806, 7259, 21732, 4226, 1588, 60, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -2.0692, -0.0174, -0.0003, -0.0001, -2.9431, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.0915, -0.0008, -1.9558, -0.1426, -0.0547, -0.0426, -0.0, -0.0545, -0.002, 0.0, -0.383, -0.0007, -0.0952, -0.0307, -1.6396, -0.1137, -0.6858, -0.0155, -0.0021, -0.0, 0.0, -2.2146, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0487, -0.0663, -1.3567, -1.8397, -0.0, -2.3822, -0.0004, 0.0, -0.16, 0.0, -0.1174, -0.0162, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.2525, -0.0449, -0.0, -0.002, -0.0001, 0.0, -1.4335, -0.0045, -0.0968, -0.0464, -3.0671, -3.781, -0.2766, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.1329, -0.77, -0.7868, -2.5884, -0.5945, -2.5585, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0046, -0.0, -20.7292, -14.604, -7.7277, -10.2084, -7.0586, -8.1688, -7.7736, -6.9936], "cumulative_logprob": -118.2504, "norm_logp": -1.4968, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 79}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 1887, 13966, 323, 7375, 4362, 369, 3259, 55149, 624, 17, 13, 65279, 279, 17975, 315, 279, 55149, 11, 2670, 14376, 11, 81887, 11, 323, 86219, 624, 18, 13, 81917, 279, 17233, 1714, 323, 894, 5871, 7096, 624, 19, 13, 39565, 17233, 3039, 323, 9315, 18564, 624, 20, 13, 24498, 10414, 369, 31045, 279, 12685, 10434, 323, 17172, 624, 21, 13, 12256, 25, 29734, 2