{"id": "434", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean tarnished jewelry at home\":\n\nTo clean tarnished jewelry at home, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth in the solution. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse it in cool water and buff it with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water and apply it with a soft, lint-free cloth. You can also use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl and submerging the jewelry in it. Let it sit for a while, then remove and rinse it with cool water. Be sure to use a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n1. Remove any dirt or debris from the jewelry using a soft, dry cloth.\n2. Mix equal parts of white vinegar and water in a small bowl. The ratio of vinegar to water should be 1:1.\n3. Dip a soft-bristled brush or an old toothbrush into the vinegar solution.\n4. Gently scrub the tarnished areas of the jewelry with the brush.\n5. Rinse the jewelry under cold water to remove any remaining vinegar and dirt.\n6. Dry the jewelry thoroughly with a soft, lint-free cloth.\n7. Store the jewelry in a dry, safe place to prevent further tarnishing.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n1. Remove any dirt or debris from the jewelry using a soft, dry cloth.\n2. Mix equal parts of white vinegar and water in a small bowl. The ratio of vinegar to water should be 1:1.\n3. Dip a soft-bristled brush or an old toothbrush into the vinegar solution.\n4. Gently scrub the tarnished areas of the jewelry with the brush.\n5. Rinse the jewelry under cold water to remove any remaining vinegar and dirt.\n6. Dry the jewelry thoroughly with a soft, lint-free cloth.\n7. Store the jewelry in a dry, safe place to prevent further tarnishing\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n1. Remove any dirt or debris from the jewelry using a soft, dry cloth.\n2. Mix equal parts of white vinegar and water in a small bowl. The ratio of vinegar to water should be 1:1.\n3. Dip a soft-bristled brush or an old toothbrush into the vinegar solution.\n4. Gently scrub the tarnished areas of the jewelry with the brush.\n5. Rinse the jewelry under cold water to remove any remaining vinegar and dirt.\n6. Dry the jewelry thoroughly with a soft, lint-free cloth.\n7. Store the jewelry in a dry, safe place to prevent further tarnishing.", "time_sec": 44.499, "generation_time_seconds": 44.4386, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0515, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.7608, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0053, -0.0004, -23.3333, -18.8947, -6.1656], "cumulative_logprob": -50.1612, "norm_logp": -3.8586, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 13}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [198, 1249, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447], "logp_list": [-0.0, -2.6983, -0.1614, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0006, 0.0, -0.0198, -1.5653, -0.0009, -0.0088, -0.0853], "cumulative_logprob": -4.5404, "norm_logp": -0.3493, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 13}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 2, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -1.7608, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.001, -0.0, -0.0053, -0.0004, -23.3333, -18.8947, -6.1656], "cumulative_logprob": -50.1612, "norm_logp": -3.8586, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 1