{"id": "518", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have the opportunity to win prizes. The specific details and mechanics of a raffle can vary. In a reverse raffle, participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, and the last ticket drawn wins the main prize. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% is allocated for a charitable purpose. In some cases, raffles may also offer additional opportunities to win prizes, such as cash tip board raffles.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe reasoning steps are:\nTo provide a detailed answer, I would need specific information about how raffles work from the passages. Since there is no such information, I cannot provide a detailed explanation or specific examples.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 10.247, "generation_time_seconds": 10.2155, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0278, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list