{"id": "615", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Passage 2 provides the necessary information to force removal of a printer in devices and printers. You can do this by first clicking on Control Panel, then selecting Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking on Printers. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you are unable to delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "pred": "The final step is to confirm the removal when prompted.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "Answer: The final step is to confirm the removal when prompted.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the printer to be removed.\n2. Open the Devices and Printers window.\n3. Locate the printer in the list.\n4. Right-click on the printer and select \"Remove device.\"\n5. Confirm the removal when prompted.\nAnswer: The final step is to confirm the removal when prompted.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: The final step is to confirm the removal when prompted.", "time_sec": 8.345, "generation_time_seconds": 8.3075, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0302, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 1249, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.0, -2.7986, -0.2708, -0.1862, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0038, -0.1325, -0.0001, -0.0005, 0.0, -0.0134, -0.7236, -0.0016, -0.1198, -0.0881, -Infinity, -16.8059, -19.5926, -12.6042, -16.3296, -5.4141, -5.9919, -4.9819, -4.4029, -3.9463, -2.222